       & ASCII.LF
       & "          <section id=""high-level-requirements-adacovex"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h1>High-Level Requirements "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " adacovex<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#high-level-requirements-adacovex"" titl"
       & "e=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""requirement-index"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Requirement Index<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#requirement-index"" title="""
       & "Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-ARCH: Architecture and build system</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-SCAN: Ada source scanning</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-PROOF: SPARK / GNATprove proof analysis</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-TEST: Test result parsing</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-COMPLIANCE: DO-178C compliance assessment (all DAL levels A-E)</p"
       & "></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-DAL-A to E: Per-level DAL criteria (see below)</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-DAL-A: DAL-A criteria "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " all HLRs traced, no orphans, tests pass, Gold SPARK</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-DAL-B: DAL-B criteria "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " all HLRs traced, no orphans, tests pass, Silver SPARK</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-DAL-C: DAL-C criteria "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " all HLRs traced, no orphans, tests pass, Bronze SPARK</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-DAL-D: DAL-D criteria "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " all HLRs traced, tests pass</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-DAL-E: DAL-E criteria "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " all HLRs traced</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-RENDER-ANSI: ANSI terminal rendering</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-RENDER-SVG: SVG badge generation</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-RENDER-MD: Markdown report generation</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-RENDER-HTML: HTML dashboard and JSON API</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-SERVER: HTTP server</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-ANSI: Terminal colour support</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-TZ: Timezone resolution and local-time formatting</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-CLI: CLI argument parsing</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-COMPLEXITY: Cyclomatic complexity and LOC gating</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-METRICS: Docstring coverage metrics</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-DIFF: Differential assessment ("
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "compare-base / "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "coverage-delta)</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-MANIFEST: Alire manifest and dependency-graph parsing</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-PROVE: GNATprove subcommand</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-SBOM: Proof-aware SBOM generation</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-IR: IR type profiles, host/target config, and foreign type-name l"
       & "owering</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""requirements"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Requirements<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#requirements"" title=""Link to th"
       & "is heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-ARCH: The tool shall build with <code class=""docutils literal not"
       & "ranslate""><span class=""pre"">alr</span> <span class=""pre"">build</span></code>"
       & " and support Makefile targets for build, prove, fmt, lint, api-docs, changel"
       & "og, and clean.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-SCAN: The tool shall recursively scan Ada source files. It shall "
       & "extract subprogram declarations, docstring annotations, and HLR traceability"
       & " tags.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-PROOF: The tool shall parse GNATprove summary output. It shall ca"
       & "tegorise verification conditions (flow, run-time, assertions, contracts, ter"
       & "mination).</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-TEST: The tool shall parse AUnit test results (Markdown or stdout"
       & "). It shall report total passed / failed test counts.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-COMPLIANCE: The tool shall assess DO-178C compliance for any DAL "
       & "level A through E. The compliance package defines and implements the assessm"
       & "ent criteria per level. The criteria appear in HLR-DAL-A through HLR-DAL-E.<"
       & "/p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-DAL-A: DAL-A assessment shall verify HLR trace coverage. All HLRs"
       & " found in source must be traced. The assessment shall find no orphan tags. A"
       & "ll tests must pass. The SPARK Gold level is the minimum requirement. All run"
       & "-time checks, assertions, functional contracts, and termination must be prov"
       & "ed.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-DAL-B: DAL-B assessment shall verify HLR trace coverage. The asse"
       & "ssment shall find no orphan tags. All tests must pass. The SPARK Silver leve"
       & "l is the minimum requirement. All run-time checks and assertions must be pro"
       & "ved. The code must be AoRTE-free.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-DAL-C: DAL-C assessment shall verify HLR trace coverage. The asse"
       & "ssment shall find no orphan tags. All tests must pass. The SPARK Bronze leve"
       & "l is the minimum requirement. Flow analysis must pass.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-DAL-D: DAL-D assessment shall verify HLR trace coverage. All test"
       & "s must pass. There is no SPARK proof requirement.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-DAL-E: DAL-E assessment shall verify HLR trace coverage only. The"
       & "re is no test or proof requirement.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-RENDER-ANSI: The tool shall render a colour-annotated summary rep"
       & "ort to standard output. It shall use ANSI escape codes.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-RENDER-SVG: The tool shall generate Shields.io-style SVG badges. "
       & "The badges show SPARK level, test status, and DO-178C compliance status.</p>"
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-RENDER-MD: The tool shall generate Markdown verification reports "
       & "(VERIFICATION.md). It shall generate traceability matrices (TRACE.md).</p></"
       & "li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-RENDER-HTML: The tool shall generate a self-contained HTML dashbo"
       & "ard page. It shall generate a JSON metrics API.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-SERVER: The tool shall serve the dashboard, API, and badge endpoi"
       & "nts. It shall use a built-in HTTP/1.1 server on a configurable port.</p></li"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-ANSI: The tool shall colour its terminal output, and shall suppre"
       & "ss colour inside CI or when NO_COLOR is set.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-TZ: The tool shall resolve a display timezone from the operating "
       & "system or from a user timezone override, and format the current date and tim"
       & "e in that zone.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-CLI: The tool shall accept CLI arguments in "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "key=value and "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "key value forms. It shall use sensible defaults. It shall print usage help o"
       & "n "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "help.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-COMPLEXITY: The tool shall compute per-file and per-subprogram cy"
       & "clomatic complexity for Ada source files. The tool shall enforce configurabl"
       & "e LOC and complexity gates. The gates cover maximum file LOC, maximum file p"
       & "ercentage of the codebase, maximum function complexity, and maximum file com"
       & "plexity.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-METRICS: The tool shall compute docstring coverage as a percentag"
       & "e of documented subprograms over total subprograms.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-DIFF: The tool shall support differential assessment via <code cl"
       & "ass=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--compare-base</span></"
       & "code>. The tool shall compare the target at a git base ref against its curre"
       & "nt working tree. The tool shall report deltas in docstring coverage, HLR tra"
       & "ceability, SPARK proof level, test results, and DAL status. The tool shall a"
       & "lso support a lightweight docstring-coverage gate via <code class=""docutils "
       & "literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--coverage-delta</span></code>.</p></"
       & "li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-MANIFEST: The tool shall resolve the project dependency graph fro"
       & "m Alire manifest files (alire.toml / alire-dev.toml). It shall resolve the a"
       & "lire.lock solved-crate list and GNAT project (.gpr) with clauses. It shall d"
       & "eduplicate results across sources.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-SBOM: The tool shall generate proof-aware software bills of mater"
       & "ials. It shall use CycloneDX 1.5 and SPDX 2.3 JSON. It shall extend every co"
       & "mponent with the adacovex:proof_level and adacovex:dal_target properties.</p"
       & "></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-PROVE: The tool shall provide a <code class=""docutils literal not"
       & "ranslate""><span class=""pre"">prove</span></code> subcommand that runs GNATpro"
       & "ve against the root .gpr file of the target project. gnatprove is not a decl"
       & "ared dependency of the tool. When the alire.toml / alire-dev.toml of the tar"
       & "get project declares a gnatprove dependency, gnatprove is resolved through A"
       & "lire (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">alr</span"
       & "> <span class=""pre"">exec</span></code>). The tool then requires only <code c"
       & "lass=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">alr</span></code> on P"
       & "ATH. Otherwise it falls back to a gnatprove on PATH, a cached ~/.adacovex/to"
       & "olchain/bin gnatprove, and finally a platform toolchain download. It transfe"
       & "rs control to the standard assessment pipeline.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>HLR-IR: The tool shall define bounded target machine-integer types. T"
       & "he types are IR_Int8 through IR_Int64 and IR_UInt8 through IR_UInt64. The to"
       & "ol shall define a host/target word-size configuration. The tool shall lower "
       & "foreign type names (int32_t, size_t, usize, and more) onto these types. The "
       & "tool shall synthesise bounded Ada declarations. GNATprove can prove these de"
       & "clarations free of integer overflow.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
