       & ASCII.LF
       & "          <section id=""adacovex-prove-patch"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h1>Adacovex.Prove_Patch<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#adacovex-prove-patch"" t"
       & "itle=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Proof patches for vendored dependencies.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The docstring patch system (Adacovex.Parsers.Source.Apply_Patches)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "overlays documentation onto vendored .ads files.  This package extends"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the same <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.adaco"
       & "vex/patches/&lt;relative-path&gt;</span></code> layout with SPARK proof"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "support.  A patch file can carry SPARK aspects.  The aspects are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SPARK_Mode on the package declaration and Pre, Post, or SPARK_Mode on"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "subprogram declarations.  The <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><sp"
       & "an class=""pre"">prove</span></code> subcommand merges them into a copy"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "of the vendored spec.  When the patch carries one, it also merges the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "vendored body.  GNATprove then analyses the vendored unit with the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "patched contracts.  It does not modify the original vendored sources."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "A .ads patch re-declares the spec with contracts.  A .adb patch opts"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the body into the proof.  The body is analysed only when it declares"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SPARK_Mode On itself.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The merge is textual and line-based.  The patched source is the original"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with each patched subprogram declaration replaced by the patch"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declaration block.  The block carries the aspects.  A declaration"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "matches on name and normalised parameter profile.  An overload patches"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "its exact signature, never a same-named sibling.  The default <code class=""d"
       & "ocutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">in</span></code> mode"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "is equivalent to a bare mode.  <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><s"
       & "pan class=""pre"">in</span> <span class=""pre"">out</span></code> and <code clas"
       & "s=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">out</span></code> are dis"
       & "tinct.  The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "package declaration is given the patch"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s package-level aspect when"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "present.  Subprogram declarations terminate at the "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(152)
       & ";"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & " of a spec"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declaration or at the <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class"
       & "=""pre"">is</span></code> of a body declaration.  A patched body"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declaration is replaced without touching the body proper.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>When the vendored body is SPARK-clean and opted in via a body patch,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "GNATprove proves the patched contracts.  When it is not, for example"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Ada.Text_IO callers, GNATprove skips the I/O bodies by design.  The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "unit is then reported as out of proof scope.  A proof patch never drags"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s proof level down."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "HLR-PROVE: GNATprove runner and proof patches</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<blockquote>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div><p><strong>Note:</strong> All items in this package are public.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div></blockquote>"
