       & ASCII.LF
       & "          <section id=""adacovex-1-10-0"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h1>adacovex 1.10.0<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#adacovex-1-10-0"" title=""Link"
       & " to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-15</em>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Version bumped 1.9.0 -&gt; 1.10.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""changes"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Changes<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#changes"" title=""Link to this heading"
       & """>"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""c1-multi-standard-compliance-abstraction-iso-26262-iec-62304"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>C1: Multi-standard compliance abstraction (ISO 26262 / IEC 62304)<a clas"
       & "s=""headerlink"" href=""#c1-multi-standard-compliance-abstraction-iso-26262-iec"
       & "-62304"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>One assessment can now satisfy DO-178C, ISO 26262, and IEC 62304 at the s"
       & "ame"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "time. A new <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">doc"
       & "s/standards.md</span></code> page maps the three standards"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & " integrity levels"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(DAL A"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "E, ASIL A"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "D/QM, and safety classes A"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "C) onto a shared rigor tier"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with the same four evidence checks adacovex already computes: HLR"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "traceability, no orphan tags, passing tests, and a minimum SPARK level.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Implemented via a <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class="
       & """pre"">Compliance_Standard</span></code> type (<code class=""docutils literal "
       & "notranslate""><span class=""pre"">DO_178C</span></code>, <code class=""docutils "
       & "literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">ISO_26262</span></code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">IEC_62304</span"
       & "></code>) with <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">"
       & "To_String</span></code> / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span c"
       & "lass=""pre"">To_Standard</span></code> conversions, a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Standard_Level_"
       & "Name</span></code> level re-labelling function, and a <code class=""docutils "
       & "literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--standard=NAME</span></code> CLI"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "flag (default <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">d"
       & "o178c</span></code>) that reuses <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"">"
       & "<span class=""pre"">--dal=LEVEL</span></code> as the shared rigor tier. A"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "new <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Assess_Stan"
       & "dard</span></code> procedure runs the same evidence checks as <code class=""d"
       & "ocutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Assess_DAL</span></code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and records the standard, so the ANSI report and SVG badge print "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "ASIL B"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Class A"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " instead of "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "DAL-C"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ".</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""c2-metric-sync-tooling-for-test-counts-and-spark-level"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>C2: Metric-sync tooling for test counts and SPARK level<a class=""headerl"
       & "ink"" href=""#c2-metric-sync-tooling-for-test-counts-and-spark-level"" title=""L"
       & "ink to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Hardcoded test counts and SPARK-level gates now have a script to keep the"
       & "m in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "sync, matching the existing proof-status script for VC counts. A new"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">tools/update-te"
       & "st-count.py</span></code> parses <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"">"
       & "<span class=""pre"">docs/test_result.md</span></code>, rewrites the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "anchored test-count phrases across AGENTS.md, README.md, Makefile, the CI"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "workflows, and <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">"
       & "agents-tree.map</span></code>, then regenerates the AGENTS.md source tree."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">tools/update-pr"
       & "oof-status.py</span></code> additionally rewrites the <code class=""docutils "
       & "literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--require-spark</span></code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">require-spark</"
       & "span></code> CI gates in the Makefile, workflows, and docs.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""c3-source-scanner-recognises-oop-modifiers-and-word-boundaries"""
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>C3: Source scanner recognises OOP modifiers and word boundaries<a class="
       & """headerlink"" href=""#c3-source-scanner-recognises-oop-modifiers-and-word-boun"
       & "daries"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
