       & ASCII.LF
       & "          <section id=""adacovex-1-28-0"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h1>adacovex 1.28.0<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#adacovex-1-28-0"" title=""Link"
       & " to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-25</em></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Version bumped 1.27.0 -&gt; 1.28.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""changes"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Changes<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#changes"" title=""Link to this heading"
       & """>"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""c1-perf-md-updated-with-measured-numbers-and-optimisation-histo"
       & "ry"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>C1: perf.md updated with measured numbers and optimisation history<a cla"
       & "ss=""headerlink"" href=""#c1-perf-md-updated-with-measured-numbers-and-optimisa"
       & "tion-history"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">docs/perf.md"
       & "</span></code> now records the 1.28.0 benchmark figures (cold ~0.6 s, warm"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "~40 ms on the self-assessment, 9.0 MiB binary / 3.6 MiB stripped), the new"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "when the numbers regress"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " workflow, and the full optimisation history in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "reverse-chronological order so each future round can see which assumption"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "drove the previous change.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""c2-stamp-fast-path-hashing-for-the-scan-cache"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>C2: Stamp fast-path hashing for the scan cache<a class=""headerlink"" href"
       & "=""#c2-stamp-fast-path-hashing-for-the-scan-cache"" title=""Link to this headin"
       & "g"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The warm-path CPU profile showed GNAT. SHA256 at ~48%: every <code class="
       & """docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.ads</span></code> file was"
       & " fully re-read and re-hashed on every run just to compute its cache key, eve"
       & "n when the content was unchanged. <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"""
       & "><span class=""pre"">Adacovex.</span> <span class=""pre"">Cache.</span> <span cl"
       & "ass=""pre"">Hash_File</span></code> now keeps an in-memory path -&gt; (size, d"
       & "igest) stamp map and serves the recorded digest without opening the file whe"
       & "n the size still matches.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The fast path is per-process (the map is not persisted), so an edited fil"
       & "e always re-hashes: its size differs or the map is empty. The same map means"
       & " the SBOM tree-walk hashing reuses the digests the source scan computed in t"
       & "he same run, collapsing two hash passes into one read plus one size check. W"
       & "arm user time dropped by roughly a third on the self-target.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""c3-sbom-system-tool-referenced-set-cache"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>C3: SBOM system-tool referenced-set cache<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#c3"
       & "-sbom-system-tool-referenced-set-cache"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Discover_Sys"
       & "tem_Dev_Deps</span></code> walked the whole project tree and word-scanned ev"
       & "ery dev-facing file on every run to collect the system-tool dev dependencies"
       & " for the SBOM. A profile showed that word scan at ~62% of warm CPU. The refe"
       & "renced-tool set is now cached on disk under a key that covers every input th"
       & "e scan reads: the content hash of exactly the files the scan reads (same <co"
       & "de class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Should_Scan</span>"
       & "</code> predicate and directory exclusions as the main walk), the curated to"
       & "ol-table names (in case the table changes within a release), and a namespace"
       & " salt. An unchanged project serves the set from one small cache blob and ski"
       & "ps the tree walk and every file read; any edit to a scanned file changes the"
       & " key and forces a re-scan.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Cold runs pay one extra tree walk (about 8% of cold); warm runs skip the "
       & "entire SBOM scan, taking the warm self-assessment from ~58 ms to ~39 ms. A u"
       & "nit test round-trips the cache: a second discovery on the same fixture and c"
       & "ache dir agrees exactly with the first, including tools that are absent from"
       & " PATH.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""c4-formal-containers-experiment-confirms-the-two-spark-mode-off"
       & "-exceptions"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>C4: Formal-containers experiment confirms the two SPARK_Mode Off excepti"
       & "ons<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#c4-formal-containers-experiment-confirms-the"
       & "-two-spark-mode-off-exceptions"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Adacovex"
       & ".Complexity</span></code> package was probed as a candidate for moving to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SPARK-approved (formal) containers so its <code class=""docutils literal notr"
       & "anslate""><span class=""pre"">SPARK_Mode</span> <span class=""pre"">(Off)</span><"
       & "/code> could be"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "removed. Scratch units under gnatprove 16.1.0 show this is not viable:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>The GNAT 16.2.1 runtime formal containers"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Ada.</span> <s"
       & "pan class=""pre"">Containers.</span> <span class=""pre"">Formal_Vectors</span></"
       & "code> and friends) are <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span clas"
       & "s=""pre"">pragma</span> <span class=""pre"">Compile_Time_Error</span></code> stu"
       & "bs; the implementations moved to the SPARK library shipped inside the gnatpr"
       & "ove toolchain (`SPARK. Containers.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Formal.*`).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>Adopting them would make the crate depend at build time on the SPARK"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "library, breaking the zero-dependency contract: gnatprove is resolved at"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "run time by the <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"""
       & ">prove</span></code> subcommand, but the containers would be a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "compile-time dependency.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>The <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Comp"
       & "lexity</span></code> aggregates embed vector components; the formal"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "containers"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & " limited private <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"
       & """>Vector</span></code> cannot be a record component, so a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cursor-iteration data-flow rewrite would be required on top of the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "library change.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Verdict recorded in <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span clas"
       & "s=""pre"">docs/proof/16.1.0-ledger.md</span></code>: <code class=""docutils lit"
       & "eral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Adacovex.</span> <span class=""pre"">Compl"
       & "exity</span></code> and <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span cla"
       & "ss=""pre"">Adacovex.</span> <span class=""pre"">Types.</span> <span class=""pre"">"
       & "Implementation</span></code> remain the only two <code class=""docutils liter"
       & "al notranslate""><span class=""pre"">SPARK_Mode</span> <span class=""pre"">(Off)<"
       & "/span></code> packages, both for the same reason (non-formal `Ada.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Containers<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">in"
       & "stantiations),</span> <span class=""pre"">and</span></code>spark-off-check` al"
       & "lows exactly these two.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""c5-makefile-parsing-moved-to-pure-python-tools"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>C5: Makefile parsing moved to pure-Python tools<a class=""headerlink"" hre"
       & "f=""#c5-makefile-parsing-moved-to-pure-python-tools"" title=""Link to this head"
       & "ing"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Several <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">make"
       & "</span></code> targets formatted or parsed text with shell one-liners that"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "broke under some shells (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span cl"
       & "ass=""pre"">awk</span></code>"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "backslash not last character on line"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ASCII.LF
       & "inside the <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">benc"
       & "h</span></code> size report) and used GNU-only filters (<code class=""docutil"
       & "s literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">grep</span> <span class=""pre"">-P</s"
       & "pan></code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">sed</span> <spa"
