       & ASCII.LF
       & "          <section id=""adacovex-1-34-0"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h1>adacovex 1.34.0<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#adacovex-1-34-0"" title=""Link"
       & " to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-29</em></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Version bumped 1.33.0 -&gt; 1.34.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""changes"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Changes<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#changes"" title=""Link to this heading"
       & """>"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""c1-overview-paired-cards-now-fill-50-50"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>C1: Overview paired cards now fill 50-50<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#c1-"
       & "overview-paired-cards-now-fill-50-50"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <strong>Doc Coverage</strong> and <strong>Dependency Scope</strong> c"
       & "ards on the Overview tab sit in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "a <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.chart-pair</"
       & "span></code> grid, but that pair was itself a single item inside the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "overview <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.chart"
       & "-grid</span></code> (auto-fit, min 280px per cell), so the two cards were"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "squeezed into one narrow column instead of each taking half the content widt"
       & "h."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The pair now spans every grid track (<code class=""docutils literal notransla"
       & "te""><span class=""pre"">grid-column:</span> <span class=""pre"">1</span> <span c"
       & "lass=""pre"">/</span> <span class=""pre"">-1</span></code>), so the two cards"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "fill 50-50 of the Overview content container exactly like <strong>Source Ove"
       & "rview</strong>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and <strong>Quick Stats</strong> do, and still stack on narrow screens.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""c2-search-finds-page-sections-not-just-tabs"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>C2: Search finds page sections, not just tabs<a class=""headerlink"" href="
       & """#c2-search-finds-page-sections-not-just-tabs"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The header search indexed each tab as one blob of words, so a query only "
       & "ever"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "jumped to a whole tab and multi-word page text such as "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "orphan tags"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " or a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "section heading rarely matched.  The index is now built from the rendered DO"
       & "M"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "at the granularity of a section:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>every <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.c"
       & "ard</span></code> / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class="""
       & "pre"">.chart-card</span></code> (labelled by its heading);</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>every compliance-table row, so "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "orphan tags"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " lands on the exact row;</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>every dependency node and every HLR-tagged element;</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>plus one catch-all entry per tab.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Queries are tokenised and every token must match (AND semantics), so mult"
       & "i-word"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "page content and section headings resolve.  Selecting a hit switches to the "
       & "tab"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<strong>and</strong> scrolls to the matched section, briefly flashing it to "
       & "show where the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "match is, instead of only switching tabs.  Dependency names, versions, scope"
       & "s,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "licences and PURLs stay indexed, so the box still filters the dependency tre"
       & "e.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""c3-system-tool-probe-cache-self-invalidates"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>C3: System-tool probe cache self-invalidates<a class=""headerlink"" href="""
       & "#c3-system-tool-probe-cache-self-invalidates"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The referenced-tools cache key now folds in every curated tool"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "version-probe flag and the probe fallback chain.  Editing how a tool"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s version"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "is read (for example the <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span cl"
       & "ass=""pre"">go</span></code> subcommand or the <code class=""docutils literal n"
       & "otranslate""><span class=""pre"">--version,</span> <span class=""pre"">-v,</span>"
       & " <span class=""pre"">version</span></code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "fallbacks) busts the cache automatically.  The 1.33-era control relied on a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manually bumped <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"""
       & ">|tools-v3|</span></code> salt; forgetting the bump silently served stale"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "probe results within a release.  No hand-maintained salt is needed now.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""c4-gnatdoc-and-gnatformat-documented-as-alire-dev-dependencies"""
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>C4: gnatdoc and gnatformat documented as Alire dev dependencies<a class="
       & """headerlink"" href=""#c4-gnatdoc-and-gnatformat-documented-as-alire-dev-depend"
       & "encies"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">gnatdoc_bin<"
       & "/span></code> and <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pr"
       & "e"">gnatformat_bin</span></code> were already dev dependencies declared in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">alire-dev.toml<"
       & "/span></code> (run via <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span clas"
       & "s=""pre"">alr</span> <span class=""pre"">exec</span></code> for the <code class="
       & """docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">make</span> <span class=""pr"
       & "e"">doc</span></code> and <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span cl"
       & "ass=""pre"">make</span> <span class=""pre"">fmt</span></code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "targets), but the README"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <em>Requirements</em> list only mentioned <code class=""docutils literal no"
       & "translate""><span class=""pre"">gnatpp</span></code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">gnatdoc</span><"
       & "/code> as optional tools.  The list now states that <strong>gnatdoc_bin</str"
       & "ong> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<strong>gnatformat_bin</strong> are managed by Alire as dev dependencies, so"
       & " the published"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "crate still installs and builds with no toolchain beyond the GNAT compiler.<"
       & "/p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""fixes"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Fixes<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#fixes"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""h1-proof-check-types-bars-now-scale-with-value"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>H1: Proof Check Types bars now scale with value<a class=""headerlink"" hre"
       & "f=""#h1-proof-check-types-bars-now-scale-with-value"" title=""Link to this head"
       & "ing"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>1.33 rolled out proof-category bars with a per-row track-width style, but"
       & " the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "CSS <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.hbar-track"
       & "</span> <span class=""pre"">{</span> <span class=""pre"">flex:</span> <span clas"
       & "s=""pre"">1</span> <span class=""pre"">}</span></code> overrode that inline widt"
       & "h, so every proof bar"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "stretched to the full row and showed only the proved <em>rate</em> (100% gre"
       & "en),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "never the magnitude "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " unlike the test-category bars, which scale because their"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "fill is measured against the largest category.  The proof fills are now also"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "measured against the largest category: the green fill is Proved/Max and the "
       & "red"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "remainder is (Checks-Proved)/Max inside a full-width track, with the grey tr"
       & "ack"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "showing the scale gap "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " so a 407-VC category reads as a longer bar than a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "56-VC one, precisely like the test chart.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""h2-links-render-in-the-accent-colour"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>H2: Links render in the accent colour<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#h2-lin"
