       & ASCII.LF
       & "as a <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">system</sp"
       & "an></code>-scope dev dependency (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate"">"
       & "<span class=""pre"">pkg:generic/mdbook</span></code>). The detection"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "stays data-driven "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " adding a tool is one table entry, and the scan remains a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "generic word-match over build files, not a hardcoded call site.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""h7-read-the-docs-build-deploys-again"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>H7: Read the Docs build deploys again<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#h7-rea"
       & "d-the-docs-build-deploys-again"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.readthe"
       & "docs.yaml</span></code> build failed in CI with <code class=""docutils litera"
       & "l notranslate""><span class=""pre"">mdbook:</span> <span class=""pre"">not</span>"
       & " <span class=""pre"">found</span></code> even"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "though <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">cargo</s"
       & "pan> <span class=""pre"">install</span> <span class=""pre"">mdbook</span></code>"
       & " succeeded. Read the Docs runs the install and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "build jobs in separate shells, and cargo writes the binary into the Rust"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "toolchain"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s bin directory, which is not on the build job"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s PATH. The build"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "command now resolves the cargo-installed <code class=""docutils literal notra"
       & "nslate""><span class=""pre"">mdbook</span></code> binary (<code class=""docutils"
       & " literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">find</span></code> under"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">$HOME</span></c"
       & "ode>) and prepends its directory to PATH before building, so the build"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "survives Rust toolchain upgrades without a hardcoded version path.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""h9-docs-search-result-links-resolve-again"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>H9: Docs search-result links resolve again<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#h"
       & "9-docs-search-result-links-resolve-again"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Clicking an mdBook search result in the bundled manual returned 404.  The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">/docs</span></c"
       & "ode> router dispatched on the query-string-stripped path (so <code class=""do"
       & "cutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">?highlight=</span></code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "reached the docs route), but the asset lookup that followed read the <em>raw"
       & "</em>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "request path, so every search result carrying <code class=""docutils literal "
       & "notranslate""><span class=""pre"">?highlight=...</span></code> (mdBook"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "mark-the-search-term parameter) was looked up in the wrong book-relative"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "shape and never found.  The docs asset key now derives from the query-stripp"
       & "ed path,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so a search-result link such as"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">/docs/usage/cli"
       & "-reference.html?highlight=serve#--serve</span></code> resolves to the page,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "then the browser"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own fragment + mark handling scrolls to the heading and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "highlights the term "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " exactly as it does under <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span c"
       & "lass=""pre"">mdbook</span> <span class=""pre"">serve</span></code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""h10-docs-pages-load-quickly-again"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>H10: Docs pages load quickly again<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#h10-docs-"
       & "pages-load-quickly-again"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The bundled manual felt slow to open: a ~15-asset page (HTML + several CS"
       & "S +"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "JS) took roughly six seconds to load.  The 4-worker server pool pinned each"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "worker to its keep-alive connection for a 5-second idle receive timeout, so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "once four sockets were held by the browser"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s parallel asset requests, the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "remaining connections queued in the accept backlog for ~5s until a worker"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "released.  The idle timeout is now half a second: a worker that finishes a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "keep-alive exchange returns to <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><s"
       & "pan class=""pre"">Accept_Socket</span></code> quickly, the burst fan-outs"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "across the pool, and a docs page loads in well under a second.  Workers are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "released faster on idle connections, which also means a stale or abandoned"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "connection is reaped sooner than before.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""h11-offline-manual-subpages-drop-their-font-links"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>H11: Offline manual subpages drop their font links<a class=""headerlink"" "
       & "href=""#h11-offline-manual-subpages-drop-their-font-links"" title=""Link to thi"
       & "s heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">tools/gen-do"
       & "cs.py</span></code> dropped the bundling-irrelevant font stylesheet link fro"
       & "m"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "each bundled page, but its pattern only matched the index page"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s un-prefixed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">fonts/</span></"
       & "code> href shape.  Subpages link the same stylesheet with a <code class=""doc"
       & "utils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">path_to_root</span></code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "prefix (for example <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class="""
       & "pre"">../fonts/</span></code>), so those kept the reference and the browser"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "issued a <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">/fonts"
       & "/...css</span></code> 404 on every subpage.  The drop now matches any"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "leading <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">../</sp"
       & "an></code> prefix, so no bundled page references the unbundled font asset.</"
       & "p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""h8-hlr-tags-are-no-longer-read-from-string-literals"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>H8: HLR tags are no longer read from string literals<a class=""headerlink"
       & """ href=""#h8-hlr-tags-are-no-longer-read-from-string-literals"" title=""Link to"
       & " this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The source scanner extracted HLR traceability tags from <code class=""docu"
       & "tils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--</span></code> sequences"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "inside string literals, treating them as comment starts. The bundled"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manual"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s generated constants embed examples such as <code class=""docutils literal n"
       & "otranslate""><span class=""pre"">--</span> <span class=""pre"">HLR-XXXX</span></c"
       & "ode> in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "HTML and JS string data, so those examples registered as orphan source"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tags and the self-assessment fell to DAL-C Unmet. The scanner now tracks"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "string literals (including <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span "
       & "class=""pre"">&quot;&quot;</span></code> escapes) and only starts a comment at"
       & " a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--</span></code"
       & "> outside one; tags inside strings are data, not traces. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "self-assessment returns to DAL-C Achieved.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""test-suite"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Test Suite<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#test-suite"" title=""Link to this h"
       & "eading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The native suite grows from 1169 to 1173 tests. The server routing catego"
       & "ry"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "adds four checks for the <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span cl"
       & "ass=""pre"">/docs</span></code> and <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"""
       & "><span class=""pre"">/docs/</span></code> routes and two near-miss paths"
       & ASCII.LF
