       & ASCII.LF
       & "          <section id=""adacovex-1-5-0"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h1>adacovex 1.5.0<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#adacovex-1-5-0"" title=""Link t"
       & "o this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Date: <em>2026-08-05</em></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Version bumped 1.4.0 -&gt; 1.5.0.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""changes"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Changes<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#changes"" title=""Link to this heading"
       & """>"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""c1-more-standard-docstring-styles"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>C1: More standard docstring styles<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#c1-more-s"
       & "tandard-docstring-styles"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The source scanner now recognises additional standard docstring conventio"
       & "ns,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "so third-party and code-generated Ada is counted correctly:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>Comment prefixes: besides the canonical <code class=""docutils literal"
       & " notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--</span>&#160; </code> (two dashes + two sp"
       & "aces),"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the single-space <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"
       & """>--</span> </code> and tab-separated (<code class=""docutils literal notrans"
       & "late""><span class=""pre"">--&lt;TAB&gt;</span></code>) styles are recognised"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "as docstrings. A bare <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class"
       & "=""pre"">--</span></code> or <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span "
       & "class=""pre"">---</span></code> divider is still not a docstring.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>Tag aliases: <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class="""
       & "pre"">&#64;parameter</span></code> == <code class=""docutils literal notransla"
       & "te""><span class=""pre"">&#64;param</span></code>, <code class=""docutils litera"
       & "l notranslate""><span class=""pre"">&#64;returns</span></code> == <code class="""
       & "docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">&#64;return</span></code>.</"
       & "p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>Summary tags: <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class="
       & """pre"">&#64;brief</span></code> and <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"
       & """><span class=""pre"">&#64;summary</span></code> mark a subprogram as document"
       & "ed.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""c2-more-test-result-formats"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>C2: More test-result formats<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#c2-more-test-re"
       & "sult-formats"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Adacovex.Par"
       & "sers.Tests</span></code> now also parses the following standard formats"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(additively with the existing Markdown-table parser):</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>TAP</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">ok</span> <spa"
       & "n class=""pre"">N</span> <span class=""pre"">-</span> <span class=""pre"">name</sp"
       & "an></code> / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">no"
       & "t</span> <span class=""pre"">ok</span> <span class=""pre"">N</span> <span class="
       & """pre"">-</span> <span class=""pre"">name</span></code> lines</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Automake</strong> test-suite "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">PASS:</span> <"
       & "span class=""pre"">name</span></code> / <code class=""docutils literal notransl"
       & "ate""><span class=""pre"">FAIL:</span> <span class=""pre"">name</span></code> lin"
       & "es</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Maven Surefire</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Tests</span> <"
       & "span class=""pre"">run:</span> <span class=""pre"">N,</span> <span class=""pre"">F"
       & "ailures:</span> <span class=""pre"">M,</span> <span class=""pre"">Errors:</span>"
       & " <span class=""pre"">E</span></code> summaries"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(failed = failures + errors)</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Unity</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">N</span> <span"
       & " class=""pre"">Tests</span> <span class=""pre"">M</span> <span class=""pre"">Failu"
       & "res</span></code> summaries (the count may be separated"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "from the word by spaces)</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""c3-longer-source-lines"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>C3: Longer source lines<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#c3-longer-source-lin"
       & "es"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Max_Line</sp"
       & "an></code> is raised from 8192 to <strong>262144</strong> characters, so sin"
       & "gle-line"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declarations from heavily code-generated projects (previously drained"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "silently) are parsed in full.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""c4-dev-manifest-proof-swap-prove-subcommand"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>C4: Dev-manifest proof swap (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate"">"
       & "<span class=""pre"">prove</span></code> subcommand)<a class=""headerlink"" href="
       & """#c4-dev-manifest-proof-swap-prove-subcommand"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>When the target project declares <code class=""docutils literal notranslat"
       & "e""><span class=""pre"">gnatprove</span></code> only in <code class=""docutils l"
       & "iteral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">alire-dev.toml</span></code> (keeping "
       & "the publishing <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">"
       & "alire.toml</span></code> clean), the <code class=""docutils literal notransla"
       & "te""><span class=""pre"">prove</span></code> subcommand now runs the proof thro"
       & "ugh a temporary shell wrapper that backs up <code class=""docutils literal no"
       & "translate""><span class=""pre"">alire.toml</span></code> / <code class=""docutil"
       & "s literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">alire.lock</span></code> / <code cl"
       & "ass=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">alire/</span></code>, s"
       & "waps the dev manifest over the publishing one, runs <code class=""docutils li"
       & "teral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">alr</span> <span class=""pre"">exec</span"
       & "> <span class=""pre"">--</span> <span class=""pre"">gnatprove</span> <span class"
       & "=""pre"">-P</span> <span class=""pre"">&lt;gpr&gt;</span></code>, and restores e"
       & "verything (via <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">"
       & "trap</span> <span class=""pre"">...</span> <span class=""pre"">EXIT</span> <span"
       & " class=""pre"">INT</span> <span class=""pre"">TERM</span></code>) even on failur"
       & "e or interruption. The assessment and SBOM pipeline always scans the publish"
       & "ing <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">alire.toml<"
       & "/span></code>, so dev-only tool declarations never leak into dependency grap"
       & "hs or SBOMs. This fixes <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span cla"
       & "ss=""pre"">make</span> <span class=""pre"">run-ada-crdt</span></code> / <code cl"
       & "ass=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">make</span> <span class"
       & "=""pre"">prove</span></code> against projects (e.g.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Ada_CRDT) that keep gnatprove out of their publishing manifest.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""c5-ir-layer-bounded-target-type-profiles"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>C5: IR layer "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " bounded target type profiles<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#c5-ir-layer-bounde"
       & "d-target-type-profiles"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>New <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">src/ir/<"
       & "/span></code> layer implements the first stage of an intermediate"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "representation for cross-compilation assessments:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Adacovex"
       & ".Target_Profiles</span></code> (SPARK On): bounded machine-integer types"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">IR_Int8</span><"
       & "/code>..<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">IR_Int6"
       & "4</span></code> (fixed-width signed ranges with <code class=""docutils litera"
       & "l notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Size</span></code> clauses) and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">IR_UInt8</span>"
       & "</code>..<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">IR_UIn"
       & "t64</span></code> (modular unsigned), plus <code class=""docutils literal not"
       & "ranslate""><span class=""pre"">Word_Size</span></code> and a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Target_Config</"
       & "span></code> record carrying <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><spa"
       & "n class=""pre"">Host_Bits</span></code> / <code class=""docutils literal notran"
       & "slate""><span class=""pre"">Target_Bits</span></code> / <code class=""docutils l"
       & "iteral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Pointer_Bits</span></code>."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Checked_Add32</"
       & "span></code> / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">"
       & "Checked_Add64</span></code> perform overflow-checked addition on the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bounded types.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Adacovex"
       & ".IR_Synthesiser</span></code> (SPARK Off, string generation): <code class=""d"
       & "ocutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">IR_Type_Name</span></code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Lower_Type_Name"
       & "</span></code> (case-sensitive: <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><"
       & "span class=""pre"">int8_t</span></code>..<code class=""docutils literal notrans"
       & "late""><span class=""pre"">uint64_t</span></code>, <code class=""docutils litera"
       & "l notranslate""><span class=""pre"">size_t</span></code>/<code class=""docutils "
       & "literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">usize</span></code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "-&gt; unsigned target-width, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><spa"
       & "n class=""pre"">isize</span></code> -&gt; signed target-width, <code class=""do"
       & "cutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">ptrdiff_t</span></code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">uintptr_t</span"
       & "></code> -&gt; pointer-width), and <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"
       & """><span class=""pre"">Synthesize_Package</span></code> that splits a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "comma/whitespace-separated type list into synthesized bounded Ada"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declarations.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Adacovex"
       & ".IR_Bounds</span></code> (SPARK On): a gnatprove fixture that derives"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">int32_t</span><"
       & "/code> / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">int64_"
       & "t</span></code> from the bounded IR types and proves the overflow"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "checks on <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Add32"
       & "</span></code> / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"
       & """>Add64</span></code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " absence of integer overflow on the lowered"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "types is machine-checked.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""c6-google-sphinx-docstring-styles"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>C6: Google / Sphinx docstring styles<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#c6-goog"
       & "le-sphinx-docstring-styles"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The source scanner now also recognises the two most common non-Ada docstr"
       & "ing"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "conventions, so the same subprogram can be documented in Ada, Google, or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Sphinx style:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Google</strong>: <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><"
       & "span class=""pre"">Args:</span></code> / <code class=""docutils literal notrans"
       & "late""><span class=""pre"">Args:</span> <span class=""pre"">...</span></code> hea"
       & "ders open a parameter block"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(deeper-indented following comment lines count as parameters); a <code class"
       & "=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Returns:</span></code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "header marks the return-value description.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Sphinx</strong>: <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><"
       & "span class=""pre"">:param</span> <span class=""pre"">Name:</span></code>, <code "
       & "class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">:parameter</span> <sp"
       & "an class=""pre"">Name:</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslat"
       & "e""><span class=""pre"">:type</span> <span class=""pre"">Name:</span></code>, <co"
       & "de class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">:return:</span></c"
       & "ode>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">:returns:</span"
       & "></code>, and <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">:"
       & "rtype:</span></code> fields are all recognised.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""fixes"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Fixes<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#fixes"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""h1-unity-summary-count-separated-by-a-space"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>H1: Unity summary count separated by a space<a class=""headerlink"" href="""
       & "#h1-unity-summary-count-separated-by-a-space"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Number_Befor"
       & "e_Word</span></code> only looked at the character immediately before the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "keyword, so <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">1</"
       & "span> <span class=""pre"">Failures</span></code> (number + space + word) parse"
       & "d as zero failures and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "overwrote the correct totals. It now skips spaces back to the preceding digi"
       & "t"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "run.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""test-suite"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Test Suite<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#test-suite"" title=""Link to this h"
       & "eading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Test suite extended: Source scanner 40 -&gt; <strong>68</strong> checks ("
       & "comment-style"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "variants, tag aliases, Google/Sphinx styles, 12000-char single-line"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declaration); Test-result parser 27 -&gt; <strong>35</strong> checks (TAP, A"
       & "utomake,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Surefire, Unity); new <strong>IR synthesis</strong> category (<strong>26</st"
       & "rong> checks). The suite"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "is now <strong>284 tests</strong>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""proof-results"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Proof Results<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#proof-results"" title=""Link to "
       & "this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Self-assessment: <strong>Platinum</strong> (36/36 VCs proved, AoRTE-free)"
       & " "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the four"
       & ASCII.LF
