       & ASCII.LF
       & "HTML document: no CDN, no network requests, works offline.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>SBOM</strong>: CycloneDX 1.5, SPDX 2.3, or Markdown format wi"
       & "th proof, standard,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and DAL/level properties</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""result-caching"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Result caching<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#result-caching"" title=""Link t"
       & "o this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex persists parsed analysis results on disk so unchanged inputs are"
       & " not re-scanned, re-parsed, or re-proved. Source scans, GNATprove summaries,"
       & " test summaries, HLR.md/LLR.md requirement parses, the resolved SBOM depende"
       & "ncy graph, and the differential-mode scans are each keyed by a namespace pre"
       & "fix plus the SHA-256 of the artifact(s) they were derived from. For example:"
       & " <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">&quot;scan:&qu"
       & "ot;</span> <span class=""pre"">|</span> <span class=""pre"">&quot;prove:&quot;</"
       & "span> <span class=""pre"">|</span> <span class=""pre"">&quot;tests:&quot;</span>"
       & " <span class=""pre"">|</span> <span class=""pre"">&quot;hlr:&quot;</span> <span "
       & "class=""pre"">|</span> <span class=""pre"">&quot;llr:&quot;</span> <span class="""
       & "pre"">|</span> <span class=""pre"">&quot;graph:&quot;</span> <span class=""pre"">"
       & "+</span> <span class=""pre"">digest</span></code>. Re-parsing a byte-identical"
       & " artifact yields a cache hit regardless of the target directory or command l"
       & "ine.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>An unchanged manifest/lockfile/.gpr set serves the cached dependency grap"
       & "h. Unchanged HLR.md/LLR.md serve the cached requirement parses. <code class="
       & """docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--compare-base</span></code"
       & "> / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--coverage-"
       & "delta</span></code> reuse cached source scans for the current tree.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Schema namespace</strong>: the default cache root is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">~/.adacovex/cac"
       & "he/&lt;version&gt;/&lt;Cache_Schema&gt;</span></code>. <code class=""docutils"
       & " literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Cache_Schema</span></code> (in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">src/core/adacov"
       & "ex-cache.ads</span></code>) is bumped whenever the serialized layout of a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cached record or the scanner/parser semantics change, so blobs written by an"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "incompatible build are never served as if valid. System-tool version probes"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "are <em>not</em> under the result cache: they live in <code class=""docutils "
       & "literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">~/.adacovex/probes/</span></code> (a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "stable machine-level store; wiping the result cache must not re-probe every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tool).</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Graph key</strong>: the dependency-graph key hashes the Alire"
       & " manifests, the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">alire.lock</spa"
       & "n></code>, every <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"
       & """>.gpr</span></code>, the vendored trees, and the root language mix."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "It also hashes the supported-language project manifests that can own a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "vendored directory (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class="""
       & "pre"">package.json</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"">"
       & "<span class=""pre"">Cargo.toml</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal no"
       & "translate""><span class=""pre"">Cargo.lock</span></code>, <code class=""docutils"
       & " literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">go.mod</span></code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">composer.json</"
       & "span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">G"
       & "emfile</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class"
       & "=""pre"">pom.xml</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><sp"
       & "an class=""pre"">pyproject.toml</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal n"
       & "otranslate""><span class=""pre"">Package.swift</span></code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and the npm lockfiles), so an edit to a test-labelled section or lockfile"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "invalidates the cached graph and the scope classification is recomputed.</p>"
       & "</li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Eviction</strong>: <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"""
       & "><span class=""pre"">Put_Cached</span></code> evicts oldest-first by modificat"
       & "ion time when more"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "than <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--cache-ma"
       & "x</span></code> entries (default <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"">"
       & "<span class=""pre"">4096</span></code>) accumulate. <code class=""docutils lite"
       & "ral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Eviction_Count</span></code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tracks removals and is reported in the ANSI cache line.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Overflow safety</strong>: <code class=""docutils literal notra"
       & "nslate""><span class=""pre"">Serialize</span></code> returns an empty blob when"
       & " a package is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "larger than <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Max"
       & "_Cache_Blob</span></code>. Callers skip storing it and <code class=""docutils"
       & " literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Deserialize</span></code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rejects empty/oversized input, so truncated data can never be served as a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "hit.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">"
       & "--target</span></code> normalization</strong>: <code class=""docutils literal"
       & " notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--target</span></code> is normalised (<code "
       & "class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.</span></code>/<code"
       & " class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">..</span></code> col"
       & "lapsed to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "a canonical absolute path) before scanning, keeping the <code class=""docutil"
       & "s literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">File_Path</span></code> values in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cached <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Package_"
       & "Info</span></code> consistent across invocations that spell the same"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "directory differently.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>CI</strong>: the GitHub action persists <code class=""docutils"
       & " literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">~/.adacovex/cache</span></code> betw"
       & "een workflow runs"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">result-cache</"
       & "span></code> input, default true).</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--no-cache</"
       & "span></code> bypasses it entirely (useful when artifacts change without thei"
       & "r"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "content hash changing, or to measure rescan cost) and <code class=""docutils "
       & "literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--cache-dir</span></code> relocates"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "it. The ANSI report shows a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">result</span> <"
       & "span class=""pre"">cache:</span> <span class=""pre"">X</span> <span class=""pre"">"
       & "hit(s),</span> <span class=""pre"">Y</span> <span class=""pre"">miss(es),</span>"
       & " <span class=""pre"">Z</span> <span class=""pre"">evicted</span></code> line per"
       & " run.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""testing"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Testing<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#testing"" title=""Link to this heading"
       & """>"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex uses a native zero-dependency test framework (<code class=""docut"
       & "ils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Adacovex.Test_Support</span></cod"
       & "e>) with 1186 tests across 16 categories. No external test framework (AUnit,"
       & " and more) is required. Test results are written to <code class=""docutils li"
       & "teral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">docs/test_result.md</span></code> in a "
       & "parseable Markdown table format.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""complexity-check"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Complexity check<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#complexity-check"" title=""Li"
       & "nk to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">complexi"
       & "ty</span></code> subcommand walks the whole target and scores many languages"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(C, C++, C#, Go, Java, JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, Ruby, PHP, Rust,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Shell, Kotlin, and the YAML/JSON/TOML/XML/Markdown/reStructuredText"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "families) alongside Ada.  Per-subprogram analysis stays Ada-specific; the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "other languages contribute file-level lines of code and decision counts."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--excludes=EXT,"
       & "EXT</span></code> skips listed file extensions and is rejected unless the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">complexity</spa"
       & "n></code> subcommand is given, so it can never run on its own.  <code class="
       & """docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">make</span> <span class=""pr"
       & "e"">complexity-check</span></code> gates the tree through the same thresholds"
       & ".</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""timezone-resolution"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Timezone resolution<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#timezone-resolution"" tit"
       & "le=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex honours the operating system"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s timezone by default.  The resolved"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "offset comes from <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pr"
       & "e"">Ada.Calendar.Time_Zones.UTC_Time_Offset</span></code>, the standard"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Ada runtime, which reads the <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><spa"
       & "n class=""pre"">TZ</span></code> variable and the system timezone through"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the C library, so the default is always the operator"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s wall clock"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(DST-aware).  <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">s"
       & "tatus</span></code> reports the effective timezone, the current date and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "time in it, and how many dated release changelogs the target carries under"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">docs/changelogs"
       & "</span></code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--tz</span><"
       & "/code> / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--time"
       & "zone</span></code> override the display zone for one invocation.  The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "value is either a well-known IANA name (for example <code class=""docutils li"
       & "teral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Asia/Singapore</span></code>) or a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "fixed <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">UTC</span"
       & "></code>/<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">GMT</s"
       & "pan></code> offset (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class="""
       & "pre"">UTC+8</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span c"
       & "lass=""pre"">GMT+8</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><"
       & "span class=""pre"">UTC+08</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notrans"
       & "late""><span class=""pre"">GMT+08</span></code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">UTC+08:30</span"
       & "></code>).  adacovex ships no timezone database, so a named zone"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "resolves from a built-in table of common IANA names and their standard-time"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "offsets.  A zone that may observe daylight saving time (marked in the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "table), or one the table lacks, is probed against the platform tzdata"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">zdump</span></"
       & "code> validates the name, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span c"
       & "lass=""pre"">date</span> <span class=""pre"">+%z</span></code> reads the current"
       & " offset, both"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "through one shell command) for the DST-correct offset; the table offset is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the fallback when the probe is unavailable.  The date/time rendering"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "compensates for GNAT"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s local-time calendar accessors, so the displayed wall"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "clock is correct in every zone.  <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"">"
       & "<span class=""pre"">HLR-TZ</span></code> covers this behaviour.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""build-and-documentation-gates"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Build and documentation gates<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#build-and-docu"
       & "mentation-gates"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Two cheap Python gates keep the dashboard and the hand-written docs in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "step with the code, and both run inside <code class=""docutils literal notran"
       & "slate""><span class=""pre"">make</span> <span class=""pre"">check</span></code>:<"
       & "/p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">tools/cs"
       & "slint.py</span></code> (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span cla"
       & "ss=""pre"">make</span> <span class=""pre"">csslint-check</span></code>) enforces"
       & " the dashboard spacing"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "convention: every <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pr"
       & "e"">margin</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span cl"
       & "ass=""pre"">padding</span></code>, and <code class=""docutils literal notransla"
       & "te""><span class=""pre"">gap</span></code> pixel length is a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "multiple of 4px.  It also runs inside <code class=""docutils literal notransl"
       & "ate""><span class=""pre"">make</span> <span class=""pre"">build</span></code>.</p"
       & "></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">tools/ch"
       & "eck-docs.py</span></code> (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span "
       & "class=""pre"">make</span> <span class=""pre"">docs-check</span></code>) fails wh"
       & "en any paragraph in the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "user docs, README, or human changelogs exceeds four sentences, and it"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rejects em dashes and Latin abbreviations (<code class=""docutils literal not"
       & "ranslate""><span class=""pre"">i.e.</span></code>, <code class=""docutils litera"
       & "l notranslate""><span class=""pre"">e.g.</span></code>, <code class=""docutils l"
       & "iteral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">etc.</span></code>)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">tools/para-spli"
       & "t.py</span></code> rewraps over-long paragraphs to comply.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The generated <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"
       & """>docs/api-docs</span></code> pages are excluded from the paragraph rule;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "its source docstrings carry the same rule.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""supported-platforms"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Supported Platforms<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#supported-platforms"" tit"
       & "le=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex supports the same platforms Alire itself supports. Because Alire"
       & " is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the packaging and delivery mechanism, adacovex inherits Alire"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "supported-platform matrix. The crate builds via <code class=""docutils litera"
       & "l notranslate""><span class=""pre"">alr</span> <span class=""pre"">build</span></"
       & "code>. It is distributed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "through the Alire community index (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate"
       & """><span class=""pre"">alr</span> <span class=""pre"">install</span> <span class="
       & """pre"">covex</span></code>). The release workflow"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "builds it with the Alire toolchain:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Binary distribution</strong>: Linux x86-64, Windows x86-64, a"
       & "nd macOS x86-64"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(the platforms for which Alire publishes binary releases and GNAT FSF"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "toolchains, including cross compilers for ARM, RISC-V, and AVR).</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>From source</strong>: any platform with a GNAT FSF 9.2+ compi"
       & "ler on which Alire"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "can be built (Alire lists FreeBSD and OpenBSD among buildable hosts).</p></l"
       & "i>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>GitHub release bundles</strong>: built on GitHub"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s Linux runners and distributed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "as <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">adacovex-vX."
       & "Y.Z.tar.gz</span></code> for every tag.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The GitHub Actions composite action pins <code class=""docutils literal no"
       & "translate""><span class=""pre"">gnat-version</span></code> (default <code class"
       & "=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">16.1.0</span></code>) via"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">alire-project/s"
       & "etup-alire</span></code>, and CI runs on <code class=""docutils literal notra"
       & "nslate""><span class=""pre"">ubuntu-latest</span></code>, so the CI-verified"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "platform is Linux x86-64. The tool itself is written in portable Ada 2012 us"
       & "ing"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "only the GNAT runtime, so no adacovex code is platform-specific beyond what "
       & "the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "GNAT runtime and Alire toolchain provide.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""delivery-and-versioning"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Delivery and Versioning<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#delivery-and-version"
       & "ing"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex follows one version across every delivery channel, and each chan"
       & "nel is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "version-locked to the same release:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Single source of truth</strong>: the <code class=""docutils li"
       & "teral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">version</span></code> field in <code cl"
       & "ass=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">alire.toml</span></code"
       & "> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">alire-dev.toml<"
       & "/span></code> is the single source, resolved by installation method. <code c"
       & "lass=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">tools/gen-version.py</"
       & "span></code> regenerates <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span cl"
       & "ass=""pre"">src/adacovex_version_info.ads</span></code> at build time (and <co"
       & "de class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">make</span> <span "
       & "class=""pre"">bump-version</span></code>). It reads the first available of <co"
       & "de class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">ADACOVEX_VERSION</"
       & "span></code> (release builds), <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><s"
       & "pan class=""pre"">alire-dev.toml</span></code> (source checkouts), or <code cl"
       & "ass=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">alire.toml</span></code"
       & "> (dependency-managed installs). For dependency-managed installs, the publis"
       & "hed crate builds from its release manifest, so the toml associated with the "
       & "covex binary for dependency management carries the version. <code class=""doc"
       & "utils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Adacovex.</span> <span class=""p"
       & "re"">Version</span></code> in <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><spa"
       & "n class=""pre"">src/adacovex.ads</span></code> re-exports the version.</p></li"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>As a result, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"""
       & ">--version</span></code>, the man page, the SBOM tool version, and the resul"
       & "t-cache namespace all derive from the manifest and can never drift. Release "
       & "builds bundle the release tag instead via the <code class=""docutils literal "
       & "notranslate""><span class=""pre"">ADACOVEX_VERSION</span></code> environment va"
       & "riable (release workflow / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span "
       & "class=""pre"">make</span> <span class=""pre"">release</span></code>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>CI is tied to the release version</strong>: the GitHub Action"
       & "s composite action"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">action.yml</sp"
       & "an></code>) is version-matched to the adacovex binary. The release workflow "
       & "bundles <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">adacove"
       & "x-vX.</span> <span class=""pre"">Y.</span> <span class=""pre"">Z.tar.gz</span></"
       & "code> and `adacovex-action-vX.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Y. Z.tar.gz<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">f"
       & "or</span> <span class=""pre"">every</span></code>vX. Y. Z<code class=""docutils"
       & " literal notranslate""> <span class=""pre"">tag,</span> <span class=""pre"">and</"
       & "span> <span class=""pre"">the</span> <span class=""pre"">action</span> <span cla"
       & "ss=""pre"">downloads</span> <span class=""pre"">the</span> <span class=""pre"">bin"
       & "ary</span> <span class=""pre"">for</span> <span class=""pre"">the</span> <span c"
       & "lass=""pre"">tag</span> <span class=""pre"">it</span> <span class=""pre"">is</span"
       & "> <span class=""pre"">referenced</span> <span class=""pre"">by</span> <span clas"
       & "s=""pre"">(</span></code>&#64;vX.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Y. Z<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""> <span class=""pre"">runs</s"
       & "pan> <span class=""pre"">that</span> <span class=""pre"">exact</span> <span clas"
       & "s=""pre"">version).</span> <span class=""pre"">Floating</span> <span class=""pre"""
       & ">tags</span> <span class=""pre"">(</span></code>vMAJOR<code class=""docutils li"
       & "teral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">,</span> </code>vMAJOR. MINOR<code clas"
       & "s=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">,</span> </code>latest<co"
       & "de class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">)</span> <span cla"
       & "ss=""pre"">are</span> <span class=""pre"">force-pushed</span> <span class=""pre"">"
       & "at</span> <span class=""pre"">release</span> <span class=""pre"">time</span> <sp"
       & "an class=""pre"">so</span> </code>&#64;latest<code class=""docutils literal not"
       & "ranslate""><span class=""pre"">/</span></code>&#64;v1<code class=""docutils lite"
       & "ral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">/</span></code>&#64;v1.3` always resolve "
       & "to the newest matching release.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>CI platform/compiler</strong>: CI validates the self-assessme"
       & "nt (build, prove,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tests) with the pinned <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span clas"
       & "s=""pre"">gnat-version</span></code> on <code class=""docutils literal notransl"
       & "ate""><span class=""pre"">ubuntu-latest</span></code>, so the CI-proven"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "combination is the released binary built against that exact toolchain.</p></"
       & "li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Attestation</strong>: every release bundle is attested with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">actions/attest<"
       & "/span></code> (OIDC), and the release notes link the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "signed attestation.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""build-time-linker-output-sframe"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Build-time linker output (SFrame)<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#build-time"
       & "-linker-output-sframe"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The Alire GNAT toolchain"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s bundled <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">ld</s"
       & "pan></code> (2.44) emits a benign message"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">error</span> <"
       & "span class=""pre"">in</span> <span class=""pre"">...(.sframe);</span> <span clas"
       & "s=""pre"">no</span> <span class=""pre"">.sframe</span> <span class=""pre"">will</s"
       & "pan> <span class=""pre"">be</span> <span class=""pre"">created</span></code>) wh"
       & "en it reads the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.sframe</span><"
       & "/code> section that newer system binutils wrote into the glibc startup"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "objects. The link still succeeds. <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"""
       & "><span class=""pre"">make</span> <span class=""pre"">build</span></code> filters"
       & " only this one message;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "all compiler and gnatprove warnings remain fully visible, so nothing real is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "ever suppressed.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""read-only"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Read Only<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#read-only"" title=""Link to this hea"
       & "ding"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex itself is read-only. It merely scans your codebase for target do"
       & "cstrings and proofs.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>It does not make edits in place or on your behalf.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""flexible"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Flexible<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#flexible"" title=""Link to this headi"
       & "ng"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex lets you write proofs and decide where proofs are pointless (for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "example code that has to involve manual memory management). You just have to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "justify your rationale. The tool is not rigid. It does not expect 100% provi"
       & "ng"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "for all use cases.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>You write the proofs yourself, so there is no magic or hidden abstraction"
       & "s here.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""pipeline-execution-order"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Pipeline (execution order)<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#pipeline-executio"
       & "n-order"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>When adacovex runs, it executes these steps in sequence:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""highlight-default notranslate""><div class=""highlight""><pre><span"
       & "></span><span class=""mf"">0.</span> <span class=""n"">Parse</span> <span class="
       & """n"">CLI</span> <span class=""n"">args</span>           <span class=""o"">-&gt;</"
       & "span> <span class=""n"">CLI_Config</span> <span class=""n"">record</span> <span "
       & "class=""p"">(</span><span class=""n"">prove</span> <span class=""o"">/</span> <spa"
       & "n class=""n"">sbom</span> <span class=""o"">/</span> <span class=""n"">diff</span>"
       & " <span class=""o"">/</span> <span class=""n"">man</span> <span class=""o"">/</span"
       & "> <span class=""n"">complexity</span> <span class=""o"">/</span> <span class=""n"""
       & ">normal</span><span class=""p"">)</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""mi"">0</span><span class=""n"">a</span><span class=""o"">.</span> <s"
       & "pan class=""n"">Early</span><span class=""o"">-</span><span class=""n"">exit</span"
       & "> <span class=""n"">modes</span>        <span class=""o"">-&gt;</span> <span cla"
       & "ss=""o"">--</span><span class=""n"">help</span> <span class=""o"">/</span> <span c"
       & "lass=""o"">--</span><span class=""n"">version</span> <span class=""o"">/</span> <s"
       & "pan class=""n"">man</span> <span class=""o"">/</span> <span class=""n"">status</sp"
       & "an> <span class=""o"">/</span> <span class=""n"">complexity</span> <span class="""
       & "n"">exit</span> <span class=""n"">before</span> <span class=""n"">the</span> <spa"
       & "n class=""n"">pipeline</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""mf"">1.</span> <span class=""n"">Determine</span> <span class=""n"">"
       & "ANSI</span> <span class=""n"">color</span>     <span class=""o"">-&gt;</span> <s"
       & "pan class=""n"">NO_COLOR</span> <span class=""n"">check</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""mf"">2.</span> <span class=""p"">(</span><span class=""n"">prove</sp"
       & "an> <span class=""n"">mode</span><span class=""p"">)</span> <span class=""n"">Run<"
       & "/span> <span class=""n"">GNATprove</span> <span class=""o"">-&gt;</span> <span c"
       & "lass=""n"">fresh</span> <span class=""n"">obj</span><span class=""o"">/</span><spa"
       & "n class=""n"">gnatprove</span><span class=""o"">/</span><span class=""n"">gnatprov"
       & "e</span><span class=""o"">.</span><span class=""n"">out</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""mf"">3.</span> <span class=""n"">Scan</span> <span class=""n"">sourc"
       & "e</span> <span class=""n"">files</span>        <span class=""o"">-&gt;</span> <s"
       & "pan class=""n"">Package_Vectors</span><span class=""o"">.</span><span class=""n"">"
       & "Vector</span> <span class=""p"">(</span><span class=""n"">subprograms</span><spa"
       & "n class=""p"">,</span> <span class=""n"">HLR</span> <span class=""n"">tags</span><"
       & "span class=""p"">,</span> <span class=""n"">docstrings</span><span class=""p"">)</"
       & "span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""mf"">4.</span> <span class=""n"">Apply</span> <span class=""n"">docs"
       & "tring</span> <span class=""n"">patches</span>  <span class=""o"">-&gt;</span> <s"
       & "pan class=""n"">Merge</span> <span class=""o"">.</span><span class=""n"">adacovex<"
       & "/span><span class=""o"">/</span><span class=""n"">patches</span><span class=""o"">"
       & "/</span> <span class=""p"">(</span><span class=""n"">strict</span> <span class="""
