       & ASCII.LF
       & "          <section id=""ai-llm-usage-in-this-project"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h1>AI / LLM Usage in this Project<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#ai-llm-usage-"
       & "in-this-project"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>This page collects everything about how AI tooling is used in the adacove"
       & "x"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "project: the disclosure, why the code is trustworthy despite AI assistance, "
       & "how"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "LLM agents are expected to work on the codebase, and the honest limits of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "machine-generated code.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""ai-assistance-disclosure"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>AI Assistance Disclosure<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#ai-assistance-discl"
       & "osure"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>AI tools were used during development for boilerplate generation, contrac"
       & "t drafting, and docstring formatting. This is stated plainly rather than hid"
       & "den. The project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own dogfood target is a zero-dependency, fully documented, SPARK-proven Ad"
       & "a codebase. AI-generated contributions must meet the same bar as hand-writte"
       & "n ones.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>That bar is 100% docstring coverage, Platinum proof, zero justified VCs, "
       & "and the full <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">ma"
       & "ke</span> <span class=""pre"">check</span></code> gate before they count.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""why-trust-this-code"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Why trust this code?<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#why-trust-this-code"" ti"
       & "tle=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Given the use of AI assistance, healthy skepticism is natural and encoura"
       & "ged."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Reliability is grounded in proof and design, not implicit trust:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Formal Verification:</strong> core Ada logic is formally veri"
       & "fied. It is Platinum"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "under <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">gnatprove"
       & "</span></code> 16.1.0, 725 VCs, 0 unproved (see"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a class=""reference internal"" href=""../proof/16.1.0-ledger.html""><span class"
       & "=""std std-doc"">docs/proof/16.1.0-ledger.md</span></a>). The proof is re-run "
       & "by"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">make</span> <sp"
       & "an class=""pre"">prove</span></code> on every change. It is a hard gate before"
       & " any release.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Read-Only Engine:</strong> adacovex assesses input payloads, "
       & "build artifacts, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "reports without modifying your source files in place. An AI-assisted tool th"
       & "at"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cannot write to the tree it audits is a smaller blast radius by design.</p><"
       & "/li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Open Auditability:</strong> fully open source under Apache-2."
       & "0. Every line, human"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "or AI-written, is inspectable.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<blockquote>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div><p><em>Still skeptical?</em> See Ken Thompson"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s landmark paper,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a class=""reference external"" href=""https://dl.acm.org/doi/epdf/10.1145/3581"
       & "98.358210""><em>Reflections on Trusting Trust</em></a>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "on the fundamental nature of trust in software toolchains. The point is that"
       & " no"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "software, compiler, or model is trustworthy purely by assertion. It must be"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "inspectable and independently verifiable.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div></blockquote>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""how-llm-agents-work-on-this-codebase"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>How LLM agents work on this codebase<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#how-llm"
       & "-agents-work-on-this-codebase"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><a class=""reference external"" href=""https://github.com/bladeacer/adacovex"
       & "/blob/main/AGENTS.md""><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class"
       & "=""pre"">AGENTS.md</span></code></a> at the repo root is the machine-readable "
       & "project"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "brief. It carries the architecture tree, the pipeline, the SPARK discipline,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the Makefile targets, and the verification gates. An agent (or human) workin"
       & "g"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "on the tree must read it first. It must follow it. In particular:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Match existing conventions</strong> and prefer editing existi"
       & "ng files. Verify"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "non-trivial changes with the project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s typecheck and tests.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Zero library dependency</strong> is a hard constraint. Use on"
       & "ly the GNAT runtime."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Keep <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">tools/*.py"
       & "</span></code> pure-stdlib, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span"
       & " class=""pre"">typing</span></code>-annotated Python.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>SPARK proof discipline</strong> (enforced by <code class=""doc"
       & "utils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">make</span> <span class=""pre"">p"
       & "rove</span></code> and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">spark-off-check"
       & "</span></code> gate): zero unproved VCs, zero justified VCs, no"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">SPARK_Mode</spa"
       & "n> <span class=""pre"">(Off)</span></code> outside the <code class=""docutils l"
       & "iteral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Types.Implementation</span></code> and"
       & " <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Complexity</sp"
       & "an></code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "container packages (non-formal <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><s"
       & "pan class=""pre"">Ada.Containers</span></code> are illegal in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SPARK_Mode-On code; see <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span cla"
       & "ss=""pre"">docs/proof/16.1.0-ledger.md</span></code>).</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>The quality gate is the contract.</strong> <code class=""docut"
       & "ils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">make</span> <span class=""pre"">che"
       & "ck</span></code> runs the same gates that"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "CI enforces before a release. A contribution that fails it is not done.</p><"
       & "/li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Generated files are regenerated, not hand-edited.</strong> Th"
       & "e version constant,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the dashboard template package, the architecture tree, the count-synced docs"
       & ","
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and the descriptions all come from <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"
       & """><span class=""pre"">tools/*.py</span></code> scripts. Their <code class=""doc"
       & "utils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--check</span></code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "modes verify they did not drift.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The doc-sync tools (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span clas"
       & "s=""pre"">tools/update-test-count.py</span></code> and <code class=""docutils l"
       & "iteral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">tools/update-proof-status.py</span></c"
       & "ode>) derive their file set from the tree itself (<code class=""docutils lite"
       & "ral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">tools/live_files.py</span></code>). They "
       & "do not use a hardcoded list. A stale metric cannot survive anywhere. Generat"
       & "ed outputs and historical records (past-release changelogs, past proof ledge"
       & "rs) are excluded.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>They keep their release-time numbers.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""verifying-claims-instead-of-trusting-them"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Verifying claims instead of trusting them<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#ve"
       & "rifying-claims-instead-of-trusting-them"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Every number in this repository"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s documentation is anchored to a generated"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "artifact, not to a human- or AI-written claim:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>VC counts and the SPARK level come from <code class=""docutils literal"
       & " notranslate""><span class=""pre"">obj/gnatprove/gnatprove.out</span></code> (v"
       & "ia"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">make</span> <sp"
       & "an class=""pre"">proof-status</span></code>).</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>Test counts come from <a class=""reference internal"" href=""../test_res"
       & "ult.html""><span class=""std std-doc"">docs/test_result.md</span></a> (via"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">make</span> <sp"
       & "an class=""pre"">test-count</span></code>).</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>Crate descriptions come from <code class=""docutils literal notranslat"
       & "e""><span class=""pre"">alire/description.txt</span></code> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">alire/long-desc"
       & "ription.txt</span></code> (via <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><s"
       & "pan class=""pre"">make</span> <span class=""pre"">description</span></code>).</p"
       & "></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The CI badge <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"""
       & ">docs/badges/*.svg</span></code> files are emitted by the assessment itself."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "If a document carries a number that does not match the artifact, one of the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--check</span><"
       & "/code> gates in <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"""
       & ">make</span> <span class=""pre"">check</span></code> fails loudly. That is the"
       & " point.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""working-in-a-fork-or-branch-llm-or-human"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Working in a fork or branch (LLM or human)<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#w"
       & "orking-in-a-fork-or-branch-llm-or-human"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Because the gates are cheap and deterministic, the safest workflow is to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "iterate locally and let <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span cla"
       & "ss=""pre"">make</span> <span class=""pre"">check</span></code> be the arbiter:</"
       & "p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""highlight-bash notranslate""><div class=""highlight""><pre><span></"
       & "span>make<span class=""w""> </span>build<span class=""w""> </span><span class=""o"
       & """>&amp;&amp;</span><span class=""w""> </span>make<span class=""w""> </span><span"
       & " class=""nb"">test</span><span class=""w"">      </span><span class=""c1""># nativ"
       & "e suite must stay 738/738</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "make<span class=""w""> </span>prove<span class=""w"">                   </span><"
       & "span class=""c1""># Platinum, 0 unproved, 0 justified</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "make<span class=""w""> </span>check<span class=""w"">                   </span><"
       & "span class=""c1""># full gate: static checks, build, test, prove,</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""w"">                             </span><span class=""c1""># doc, "
       & "sbom, then tree-wide count-sync checks</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</pre></div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">make</span> "
       & "<span class=""pre"">check</span></code> runs the cheap static gates first (asc"
       & "ii, spark-off, changelog, version source, doc links). A formatting or sync p"
       & "roblem fails before the expensive build and SPARK proof. Then it verifies th"
       & "e count-sync checks (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class="
       & """pre"">test-count</span> <span class=""pre"">--check</span></code>, <code class"
       & "=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">proof-status</span> <span "
       & "class=""pre"">--check</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"
       & """><span class=""pre"">description</span> <span class=""pre"">--check</span></cod"
       & "e>). A stale metric anywhere in the tree fails loudly.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Regenerated files that are byte-identical when nothing changed (the versi"
       & "on constant, the dashboard template) are left untouched. <code class=""docuti"
       & "ls literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">git</span> <span class=""pre"">statu"
       & "s</span></code> stays quiet.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""the-served-dashboard-as-a-trust-surface"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>The served dashboard as a trust surface<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#the-"
       & "served-dashboard-as-a-trust-surface"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">adacovex</sp"
       & "an> <span class=""pre"">--serve</span></code> renders a live HTML dashboard at"
       & " <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">/</span></code"
       & ">. It also renders a JSON API at <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"">"
       & "<span class=""pre"">/api/metrics</span></code> and SVG badges at <code class="""
       & "docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">/badge/*.svg</span></code>. "
       & "The same numbers that an agent or reviewer quotes from the CLI are visible a"
       & "nd machine-checkable in the browser. The dashboard shell is a real file (<co"
       & "de class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">resources/dashboar"
       & "d.html</span></code>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>It is bundled at build time by <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"""
       & "><span class=""pre"">tools/gen-dashboard.py</span></code>. Page chrome is a pl"
       & "ain HTML edit with no Ada knowledge required. The dynamic cards are injected"
       & " by the Ada renderer. The theme resolution chain (query param, then explicit"
       & " <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--theme</span>"
       & "</code>, then saved <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class="""
       & "pre"">localStorage</span></code>, then system preference) and the localStorag"
       & "e-only persistence are documented in <a class=""reference internal"" href=""../"
       & "usage/dashboard.html""><span class=""std std-doc"">dashboard.md</span></a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""honest-limits"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Honest limits<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#honest-limits"" title=""Link to "
       & "this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>AI assistance raises the pace of contribution but does not change the bar"
       & ":</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>An AI-written docstring that is not provably accurate is a liability,"
       & " not a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "contribution. The 100% docstring-coverage gate measures presence. Review"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "measures accuracy.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>Generated code must still pass the SPARK proof. A <code class=""docuti"
       & "ls literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">pragma</span> <span class=""pre"">As"
       & "sume</span></code> or a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">SPARK_Mode</spa"
       & "n> <span class=""pre"">(Off)</span></code> outside the two allowed container p"
       & "ackages is rejected"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "by the gates.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>The changelog, the traceability tags, and the HLRs are written by peo"
       & "ple."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "They are also written by agents following AGENTS.md. The <code class=""docuti"
       & "ls literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">changelog-check</span></code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "validator enforces the canonical format. A machine-generated changelog that"
       & ASCII.LF
