       & ASCII.LF
       & "          <section id=""performance"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h1>Performance<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#performance"" title=""Link to this"
       & " heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex is a zero-dependency CLI. Its hot path is the assessment pipelin"
       & "e"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(scan -&gt; patch -&gt; doc metrics -&gt; proof parse -&gt; test parse -&gt;"
       & " DAL assess -&gt;"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "render, plus the SBOM). This page documents how to benchmark it. It also"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "documents the expected numbers on a typical machine and the optimisations"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "that keep those numbers low.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""benchmarking"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Benchmarking<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#benchmarking"" title=""Link to th"
       & "is heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">make</span> "
       & "<span class=""pre"">bench</span></code> benchmarks the assessment pipeline and"
       & " reports binary size:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>It builds the project, then times <code class=""docutils literal notra"
       & "nslate""><span class=""pre"">./bin/adacovex</span></code> against the repo itse"
       & "lf.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>cold</strong> runs (fresh result cache + probe cache) and <st"
       & "rong>warm</strong> runs"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(populated caches) are measured separately.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">make</sp"
       & "an> <span class=""pre"">bench</span></code> uses <a class=""reference external"""
       & " href=""https://github.com/sharkdp/hyperfine"">hyperfine</a> when"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "installed. It falls back to the bash <code class=""docutils literal notransla"
       & "te""><span class=""pre"">time</span></code> builtin otherwise. No tooling is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "required.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>It samples generously so the reported mean is stable. Hyperfine runs "
       & "<strong>10"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cold + 15 warm</strong> repetitions (2 warmup runs). Each cold repetition de"
       & "letes"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the cache dir first. This measures a truly empty result and probe cache. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">time</span></co"
       & "de> fallback runs <strong>5 cold + 5 warm</strong>.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>It reports the raw and stripped binary sizes (the stripped size is me"
       & "asured"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "on a <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">/tmp</span"
       & "></code> copy; the build output is never modified).</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Example output (hyperfine, x86-64, 8-core CI-class machine, 1.28.0):</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""highlight-default notranslate""><div class=""highlight""><pre><span"
       & "></span><span class=""o"">===</span> <span class=""n"">Cold</span> <span class="""
       & "p"">(</span><span class=""n"">fresh</span> <span class=""n"">result</span> <span "
       & "class=""n"">cache</span><span class=""p"">)</span> <span class=""o"">===</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "  <span class=""n"">Time</span> <span class=""p"">(</span><span class=""n"">mean</"
       & "span> <span class=""o"">+/-</span> <span class=""n"">sigma</span><span class=""p"""
       & ">):</span>  <span class=""mf"">88.1</span> <span class=""n"">ms</span> <span cla"
       & "ss=""o"">+/-</span> <span class=""mf"">3.8</span> <span class=""n"">ms</span>   <s"
       & "pan class=""p"">[</span><span class=""n"">User</span><span class=""p"">:</span> <s"
       & "pan class=""mf"">62.1</span> <span class=""n"">ms</span><span class=""p"">,</span>"
       & " <span class=""n"">System</span><span class=""p"">:</span> <span class=""mf"">14.0"
       & "</span> <span class=""n"">ms</span><span class=""p"">]</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "  <span class=""n"">Range</span> <span class=""p"">(</span><span class=""nb"">min<"
       & "/span> <span class=""o"">...</span> <span class=""nb"">max</span><span class=""p"""
       & ">):</span>    <span class=""mf"">84.8</span> <span class=""n"">ms</span> <span c"
       & "lass=""o"">...</span> <span class=""mf"">96.4</span> <span class=""n"">ms</span>  "
       & "  <span class=""mi"">10</span> <span class=""n"">runs</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""o"">===</span> <span class=""n"">Warm</span> <span class=""p"">(</sp"
       & "an><span class=""n"">populated</span> <span class=""n"">caches</span><span class"
       & "=""p"">)</span> <span class=""o"">===</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "  <span class=""n"">Time</span> <span class=""p"">(</span><span class=""n"">mean</"
       & "span> <span class=""o"">+/-</span> <span class=""n"">sigma</span><span class=""p"""
       & ">):</span>  <span class=""mf"">34.2</span> <span class=""n"">ms</span> <span cla"
       & "ss=""o"">+/-</span> <span class=""mf"">2.3</span> <span class=""n"">ms</span>   <s"
       & "pan class=""p"">[</span><span class=""n"">User</span><span class=""p"">:</span> <s"
       & "pan class=""mf"">15.3</span> <span class=""n"">ms</span><span class=""p"">,</span>"
       & " <span class=""n"">System</span><span class=""p"">:</span> <span class=""mf"">8.7<"
       & "/span> <span class=""n"">ms</span><span class=""p"">]</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "  <span class=""n"">Range</span> <span class=""p"">(</span><span class=""nb"">min<"
       & "/span> <span class=""o"">...</span> <span class=""nb"">max</span><span class=""p"""
       & ">):</span>    <span class=""mf"">30.9</span> <span class=""n"">ms</span> <span c"
       & "lass=""o"">...</span> <span class=""mf"">39.2</span> <span class=""n"">ms</span>  "
       & "  <span class=""mi"">15</span> <span class=""n"">runs</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""o"">==</span> <span class=""n"">Binary</span> <span class=""n"">size"
       & "</span> <span class=""o"">==</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""nb"">bin</span><span class=""o"">/</span><span class=""n"">adacovex<"
       & "/span>            <span class=""mf"">9.0</span> <span class=""n"">MiB</span> <sp"
       & "an class=""p"">(</span><span class=""mi"">9461040</span> <span class=""nb"">bytes<"
       & "/span><span class=""p"">)</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""n"">after</span> <span class=""n"">strip</span>             <span "
       & "class=""mf"">4.3</span> <span class=""n"">MiB</span> <span class=""p"">(</span><sp"
       & "an class=""mi"">4463704</span> <span class=""nb"">bytes</span><span class=""p"">)<"
       & "/span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""n"">savings</span>                 <span class=""mf"">52.8</span><"
       & "span class=""o"">%</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</pre></div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The numbers shift with the machine and the codebase. What matters is the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "shape: warm is now in the tens of milliseconds, and the cold path is bounded"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "by the work that genuinely must happen (hashing the changed sources and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "building the SBOM).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>For single-shot timings, plain <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"""
       & "><span class=""pre"">time</span></code> works the same way:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""highlight-bash notranslate""><div class=""highlight""><pre><span></"
       & "span><span class=""nb"">time</span><span class=""w""> </span>./bin/adacovex<span"
       & " class=""w""> </span>--no-cache<span class=""w"">          </span><span class=""c"
       & "1""># cold, no result cache</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""nb"">time</span><span class=""w""> </span>./bin/adacovex<span clas"
       & "s=""w""> </span>--cache-dir<span class=""o"">=</span>/tmp/c<span class=""w"">  </s"
       & "pan><span class=""c1""># warm</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</pre></div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>When you compare two versions, always reset the cache between runs. Use"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--cache-dir=&lt"
       & ";fresh</span> <span class=""pre"">dir&gt;</span></code> or delete the cache di"
       & "r. The result cache must not"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "hide the real cost.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">make</span> "
       & "<span class=""pre"">perf-bench</span></code> profiles CPU and syscalls directl"
       & "y with <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">perf</sp"
       & "an></code> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">strace</span></"
       & "code> over <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">bin/"
       & "adacovex</span></code>. It prints the cache-miss rates and the syscall"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "counts so a regression in I/O or data layout is visible before a release.</p"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""what-the-numbers-mean"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>What the numbers mean<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#what-the-numbers-mean"""
       & " title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Figures below are from <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span c"
       & "lass=""pre"">make</span> <span class=""pre"">bench</span></code>/<code class=""do"
       & "cutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">perf-bench</span></code> on th"
       & "is machine (hyperfine,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cold + warm, 2 warmup). They shift with the machine and the codebase. What"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "matters is the shape:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Cold ~0.1 s</strong>: dominated by source scanning (Ada file "
       & "enumeration and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SHA-256 of every scanned file), the SBOM tree walk and word scan, and the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "renderers. Nothing here can be skipped: the result cache is empty, so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "every file must be read and hashed at least once. The system-tool version"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "probes are <em>not</em> part of cold anymore (they live per-machine and are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cached across cache wipes).</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Warm ~35 ms</strong>: the on-disk result cache (content-addre"
       & "ssed per file,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "oldest-first eviction) skips re-parsing unchanged sources. The stamp"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "fast-path skips the per-file SHA-256 entirely (a file unchanged in size is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "not re-hashed). The tools-set cache skips the whole SBOM dev-dependency"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "word scan and the tool probes for an unchanged project. The remaining"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "time is process startup (dynamic loader hwcaps probing, elaboration), the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "directory walks, and the blob deserialization.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>System time is the tell. Cold runs show ~13 ms of system time (file I"
       & "/O);"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "warm runs show ~9 ms.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""optimisation-history"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Optimisation history<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#optimisation-history"" t"
       & "itle=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Kept in reverse-chronological order.  Every entry names the measurement t"
       & "hat"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "drove it so the next round of work can see whether the previous assumption"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "still holds.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""stamp-fast-path-hashing-1-28-0"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>Stamp fast-path hashing (1.28.0)<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#stamp-fast-"
       & "path-hashing-1-28-0"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The warm-path profile showed GNAT. SHA256 at ~48% of CPU: every <code cla"
       & "ss=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.ads</span></code> file "
       & "was fully re-read and re-hashed on every run just to compute its cache key, "
       & "even though the content was unchanged. <code class=""docutils literal notrans"
       & "late""><span class=""pre"">Hash_File</span></code> now keeps an in-memory map o"
       & "f path -&gt; (size, digest). A file whose size still matches the recorded si"
       & "ze serves the recorded digest without opening or reading the file. The fast "
       & "path is used only within one process (the map is not persisted), so a conten"
       & "t change is always caught (the size differs or the map is empty).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The same fast path serves the SBOM tree-walk hashing, which re-hashes fil"
       & "es the source scan already touched in the same run (the two hash passes coll"
       & "apse into one real read + one size check). Warm user time dropped roughly a "
       & "third.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""stable-probe-store-probe-results-in-the-tools-blob-1-28-0"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>Stable probe store + probe results in the tools blob (1.28.0)<a class=""h"
       & "eaderlink"" href=""#stable-probe-store-probe-results-in-the-tools-blob-1-28-0"""
       & " title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The cold profile was dominated by the system-tool version probes: each"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "spawns a subprocess, and node/hg/mandb boot an interpreter (hg alone cost"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "~330 ms on this machine; the full probe set ~150 ms end to end). The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "probes were kept under the <em>result</em> cache (<code class=""docutils lite"
       & "ral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">&lt;cache-dir&gt;/probes/</span></code>),"
       & " so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "wiping the cache (or pointing <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><sp"
       & "an class=""pre"">--cache-dir</span></code> elsewhere) re-probed every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tool.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Two changes removed that cost:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>Probes now live in <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span c"
       & "lass=""pre"">~/.adacovex/probes/</span></code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a stable, machine-level"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "store external to the result cache. Wiping the result cache (or using a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "fresh <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--cache-d"
       & "ir</span></code>) no longer re-probes; only the 7-day TTL ever"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "re-probes a known toolchain. Cold on a warm-probe machine dropped from"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "~658 ms to ~86 ms (7.7 x).</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>The tools-set cache blob now also stores each referenced tool"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s probe"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "result (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">tool=ve"
       & "rsion</span></code> pairs), and a cache hit rebuilds the SBOM tool"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "edges from those pairs without PATH lookups, probe file reads, or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "subprocess spawns. Warm dropped from ~39.8 ms to ~34.6 ms. The blob"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "format is names-<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"""
       & ">|</span></code>-version-pairs; <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><"
       & "span class=""pre"">Cache_Schema</span></code> was bumped to s6 so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "old names-only blobs are never served as if complete. Cold and warm"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "SBOM output stays byte-identical.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""file-stamp-fast-path-and-eviction-batching-1-27-0"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>File-stamp fast-path and eviction batching (1.27.0)<a class=""headerlink"""
       & " href=""#file-stamp-fast-path-and-eviction-batching-1-27-0"" title=""Link to th"
       & "is heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Put_Cached</"
       & "span></code> ran eviction after every store; eviction walks the whole cache"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tree. It now runs every 32 stores (bounded overshoot under the soft cap)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The SBOM dev-dependency word scan was rewritten from a per-tool substring"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "match (60 tools x line length) to a single-pass word extraction (per-word x"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "distinct tool lengths), and tool-output directories (<code class=""docutils l"
       & "iteral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">gnatprove/</span></code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">__pycache__</sp"
       & "an></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">nod"
       & "e_modules</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span cl"
       & "ass=""pre"">.headroom</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"
       & """><span class=""pre"">.lccst</span></code>) were excluded from"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "both tree walks so the proof-run output is not enumerated. Those changes"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "alone took the warm run from ~1.02 s to ~63 ms (16x) and cold from ~1.4 s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "to ~545 ms, and reduced the warm-run syscall count from ~15k to ~12k.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""probe-cache"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>Probe cache<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#probe-cache"" title=""Link to this"
       & " heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><em>(Origin story.)</em> The SBOM builds a <em>dev-scope</em> dependency "
       & "edge for every tool that the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s build references. The tool must be installed on <code class=""docutils lite"
       & "ral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">$PATH</span></code> (for example <code cl"
       & "ass=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">gcc</span></code>, <cod"
       & "e class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">alr</span></code>, "
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">git</span></cod"
       & "e>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">make</span>"
       & "</code>). The SBOM probes each tool with <code class=""docutils literal notra"
       & "nslate""><span class=""pre"">&lt;tool&gt;</span> <span class=""pre"">&lt;flag&gt;"
       & "</span></code> to capture its version. Each probe spawns a subprocess.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The subprocess costs tens of milliseconds per referenced tool (<code clas"
       & "s=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">System:</span> <span clas"
       & "s=""pre"">42</span> <span class=""pre"">ms</span> <span class=""pre"">-&gt;</span>"
       & " <span class=""pre"">9</span> <span class=""pre"">ms</span></code>, ~150 ms end "
       & "to end on an 11-tool toolchain). Originally the probed versions were cached "
       & "under <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">&lt;cache"
       & "-root&gt;/probes/&lt;tool&gt;</span></code> with a 7-day TTL. That location "
       & "meant a wiped result cache re-probed every tool on the next run "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " which is why 1.28.0 moved the store and folded the probe results into the t"
       & "ools-set cache blob (see above).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""binary-size"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Binary size<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#binary-size"" title=""Link to this"
       & " heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The debug-symbol-carrying build is ~9 MiB. Stripping (<code class=""docuti"
       & "ls literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">strip</span> <span class=""pre"">bin"
       & "/adacovex</span></code>) yields ~3.6 MiB (~60% smaller) without affecting be"
       & "haviour. GNAT"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s default build keeps symbols for debugging (<code class=""docutils literal n"
       & "otranslate""><span class=""pre"">gdb</span></code> works). Release artifacts ar"
       & "e stripped. <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">mak"
       & "e</span> <span class=""pre"">bench</span></code> always reports both.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Regressions in code size are visible in the same command that reports tim"
       & "ings. If the symbols ever come out, the binary size is the same and the page"
       & " should say so.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""ci"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>CI<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#ci"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>CI runs the self-assessment with result caching disabled where determinis"
       & "m matters (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--no"
       & "-cache</span></code>-equivalent fresh dirs). The <code class=""docutils liter"
       & "al notranslate""><span class=""pre"">make</span></code> gates are timed loosely"
       & ". Timings are informational only. The <code class=""docutils literal notransl"
       & "ate""><span class=""pre"">bench</span></code> target is not part of <code class"
       & "=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">make</span> <span class=""p"
       & "re"">check</span></code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>It makes the gate machine-dependent. A slow CI runner must not fail a bui"
       & "ld. The target is run by hand before releases.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""when-the-numbers-regress"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>When the numbers regress<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#when-the-numbers-re"
       & "gress"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Run <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">make</sp"
       & "an> <span class=""pre"">perf-bench</span></code> first. It reports the CPU bre"
       & "ak-down (the wall-clock"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">perf</span></co"
       & "de> output) and the strace syscall counts. The single-reader/single-writer"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cache walks are the usual suspects: a new tree walk that re-enumerates a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "directory which a cache already covers, or a new per-file hash that the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "stamp fast path does not cover. The numbers in this page are from the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "self-assessment; the Ada_CRDT target is smaller and exercises the same"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "pipeline, so <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">ma"
       & "ke</span> <span class=""pre"">run-ada-crdt</span></code> is a handy second dat"
       & "apoint.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "        </article>"
