       & "              <svg class=""theme-icon-when-light""><use href=""#svg-sun""></use>"
       & "</svg>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "            </button>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "          </div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "          <label class=""toc-overlay-icon toc-content-icon"" for=""__toc"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "            <span class=""icon""><svg><use href=""#svg-toc""></use></svg></span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "          </label>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "        </div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "        <article role=""main"" id=""furo-main-content"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "          <section id=""proving-and-writing-spark-proofs"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h1>Proving and writing SPARK proofs<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#proving-and"
       & "-writing-spark-proofs"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex runs gnatprove, reads its summary, and grades the result against"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the <a class=""reference internal"" href=""../api-docs/adacovex-spark-levels.ht"
       & "ml""><span class=""std std-doc"">SPARK assurance levels</span></a>. This page"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "is the guide to both halves: <strong>how proving works</strong> under adacov"
       & "ex, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<strong>how to write proofs</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " contracts in your own code, and "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " when the code"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "is vendored and cannot be modified "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <strong>proof patches</strong> that add the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "contracts for you.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""proving-a-project-with-adacovex"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Proving a project with adacovex<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#proving-a-pr"
       & "oject-with-adacovex"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""highlight-bash notranslate""><div class=""highlight""><pre><span></"
       & "span>adacovex<span class=""w""> </span>prove<span class=""w""> </span>--target<s"
       & "pan class=""o"">=</span>."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</pre></div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">prove</s"
       & "pan></code> subcommand (full options:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a class=""reference internal"" href=""../usage/cli-reference.html#the-prove-su"
       & "bcommand""><span class=""std std-ref"">CLI reference "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">prove</spa"
       & "n></code> subcommand</span></a>):</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol class=""arabic simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Resolves gnatprove</strong> without requiring the target to d"
       & "eclare it:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manifest pin &gt; global pin &gt; <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"""
       & "><span class=""pre"">$PATH</span></code> &gt; cached toolchain &gt; download. "
       & "Full"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "order and per-method detail:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a class=""reference internal"" href=""architecture.html#gnatprove-toolchain-re"
       & "solution-prove-subcommand""><span class=""std std-ref"">Architecture "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " GNATprove toolchain resolution</span></a>.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Runs gnatprove</strong> against the target (or against a patc"
       & "hed tree copy"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "when proof patches are present "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " see"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a class=""reference internal"" href=""#proof-patches-proving-vendored-dependen"
       & "cies"">Proof patches</a> below) and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "writes the summary to <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class"
       & "=""pre"">&lt;target&gt;/obj/gnatprove/gnatprove.out</span></code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the same"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "location the assessment pipeline discovers.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Falls through to the full assessment</strong>. The assessment"
       & " parses the fresh"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "summary. One command both proves and assesses. The <code class=""docutils lit"
       & "eral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--require-*</span></code> CI gates"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "apply to the proof run directly (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate"">"
       & "<span class=""pre"">--require-spark=Platinum</span> <span class=""pre"">--requir"
       & "e-proof=100</span></code> and more; see"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a class=""reference internal"" href=""../usage/cli-reference.html#ci-threshold"
       & "-gates-require""><span class=""std std-ref"">CLI reference "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " CI threshold gates</span></a>).</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The result cache serves unchanged targets so repeated runs are cheap."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--force</span><"
       & "/code> bypasses the cache and forces a full gnatprove reanalysis. A target"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "without a <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">gnatp"
       & "rove.out</span></code> at all is graded <code class=""docutils literal notran"
       & "slate""><span class=""pre"">Stone</span></code> with proof metrics <code class="
       & """docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">N/A</span></code>."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Run <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">prove</span"
       & "></code> to generate one.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""what-a-proof-contains"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>What a proof contains<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#what-a-proof-contains"""
       & " title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>gnatprove reports verification conditions (VCs) per check category. The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "summary in <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">gnat"
       & "prove.out</span></code> breaks them down as:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper colwidths-auto docutils container"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table class=""docutils align-default"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><th class=""head""><p>Category</p></th>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<th class=""head""><p>What it covers</p></th>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-even""><td><p>Run-time checks</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Index bounds, overflow, division-by-zero, range checks "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " absence of run-time errors</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><td><p>Assertions</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>User <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">pra"
       & "gma</span> <span class=""pre"">Assert</span></code> statements and pre/postcon"
       & "dition checks</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-even""><td><p>Functional contracts</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Pre</spa"
       & "n></code> / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Pos"
       & "t</span></code> / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pr"
       & "e"">Global</span></code> contract satisfaction</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><td><p>Data dependencies</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Flow analysis: uninitialized reads, effective <code class=""docutils l"
       & "iteral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Global</span></code> contracts</p></td"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-even""><td><p>Initialization</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>All objects initialized before first use</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><td><p>Termination</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Loop_Var"
       & "iant</span></code> / recursion bounds (subprograms proved terminating)</p></"
       & "td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The honest <strong>proved</strong> count is <code class=""docutils literal"
       & " notranslate""><span class=""pre"">total</span> <span class=""pre"">-</span> <spa"
       & "n class=""pre"">justified</span> <span class=""pre"">-</span> <span class=""pre"">"
       & "unproved</span></code> (flow plus"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "provers). The <a class=""reference internal"" href=""../api-docs/adacovex-spark"
       & "-levels.html""><span class=""std std-doc"">assurance level</span></a> is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "derived from how many of each category were discharged:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Stone</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " no proof run or nothing analyzable;</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Bronze</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " flow analysis clean (data dependencies, initialization);</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Silver</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " run-time checks proved, assertions proved;</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Gold</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " functional contracts proved on top;</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Platinum</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " every VC proved: <strong>0 unproved</strong> (and, in adacovex"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gate, <strong>0 justified</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " no <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">pragma</spa"
       & "n> <span class=""pre"">Annotate</span></code> justifications).</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Justified VCs count neither as proved nor as unproved. Only unproved VCs"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "downgrade the level. For a DAL assessment, the level must meet the requireme"
       & "nt"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "of the tier (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--"
       & "dal=C</span></code> needs Bronze, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"""
       & "><span class=""pre"">--dal=A</span></code> needs Gold, and more) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " see"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a class=""reference internal"" href=""../api-docs/adacovex-dal-levels.html""><s"
       & "pan class=""std std-doc"">DAL levels</span></a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""writing-proofs-spark-contracts"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Writing proofs: SPARK contracts<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#writing-proo"
       & "fs-spark-contracts"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A proof starts with contracts in the source, written as Ada aspects:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""highlight-ada notranslate""><div class=""highlight""><pre><span></s"
       & "pan><span class=""kd"">package</span> <span class=""kd"">Body</span><span class="
       & """nc"">_Vec</span> <span class=""kr"">is</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   <span class=""kd"">function</span> <span class=""nf"">Clamp</span> <span clas"
       & "s=""p"">(</span><span class=""nv"">Value</span> <span class=""p"">: </span><span c"
       & "lass=""nv"">in</span> <span class=""nv"">Integer</span><span class=""p"">;</span> "
       & "<span class=""nv"">Lo</span> <span class=""p"">: </span><span class=""nv"">in</spa"
       & "n> <span class=""nv"">Integer</span><span class=""p"">;</span> <span class=""nv"">"
       & "Hi</span> <span class=""p"">: </span><span class=""nv"">in</span> <span class=""n"
       & "v"">Integer</span><span class=""p"">)</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "     <span class=""kr"">return</span> <span class=""kt"">Integer</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "     <span class=""kn"">with</span> <span class=""n"">Pre</span>  <span class=""p"
       & """>=&gt;</span> <span class=""n"">Lo</span> <span class=""o"">&lt;=</span> <span "
       & "class=""n"">Hi</span><span class=""p"">,</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "          <span class=""n"">Post</span> <span class=""p"">=&gt;</span> <span cla"
       & "ss=""n"">Clamp</span><span class=""p"">'</span><span class=""na"">Result</span> <s"
       & "pan class=""ow"">in</span> <span class=""n"">Lo</span> <span class=""p"">..</span>"
       & " <span class=""n"">Hi</span><span class=""p"">;</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""kr"">end</span> <span class=""nf"">Body_Vec</span><span class=""p"">"
       & ";</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</pre></div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Rules that matter in practice:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">"
       & "SPARK_Mode</span> <span class=""pre"">=&gt;</span> <span class=""pre"">On</span>"
       & "</code> selects what gnatprove analyses.</strong> Without it a unit"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "is out of proof scope. It can be declared on the package"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">package</span>"
       & " <span class=""pre"">P</span> <span class=""pre"">with</span> <span class=""pre"">"
       & "SPARK_Mode</span> <span class=""pre"">=&gt;</span> <span class=""pre"">On</span>"
       & " <span class=""pre"">is</span></code>), on individual subprograms, or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "both "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " adacovex"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own source uses package-level On on pure units and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "per-subprogram On aspects inside default-off bodies.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>A body is analysed only when the body itself opts in.</strong"
       & "> Declaring"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">SPARK_Mode</spa"
       & "n> <span class=""pre"">=&gt;</span> <span class=""pre"">On</span></code> on the "
       & "<em>spec</em> does not make gnatprove analyse the body."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The body must declare it too (on the <code class=""docutils literal notransla"
       & "te""><span class=""pre"">package</span> <span class=""pre"">body</span></code> li"
       & "ne or per subprogram)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "This is the rule that makes proof patches necessary for vendored code "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " see"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "below.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>I/O bodies are skipped by design.</strong> A body that calls "
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Ada.Text_IO</sp"
       & "an></code> (which"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "is <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">SPARK_Mode</"
       & "span> <span class=""pre"">Off</span></code>) cannot be analysed. gnatprove rep"
       & "orts the unit out of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proof scope. This never drags the assessed level down "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " it means those"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bodies are not proved.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Contracts are proved against the body.</strong> gnatprove pro"
       & "ves that every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "possible body execution satisfies the declared <code class=""docutils literal"
       & " notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Pre</span></code>/<code class=""docutils lite"
       & "ral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Post</span></code>. Callers must in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "turn establish the <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""p"
       & "re"">Pre</span></code> before calling.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">"
       & "--steps</span></code> controls the proof budget.</strong> gnatprove"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s default step limit can"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "produce solver-timeout false negatives. adacovex runs with <code class=""docu"
       & "tils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--steps</span> <span class=""pre"""
       & ">10000</span></code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "by default so such timeouts are not reported as unproved. An explicit"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--steps=N</span"
       & "></code> overrides.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The goal for a clean proof: every VC in every category proved, 0 unproved"
       & ","
       & ASCII.LF
       & "0 justified.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""proof-patches-proving-vendored-dependencies"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Proof patches: proving vendored dependencies<a class=""headerlink"" href="""
       & "#proof-patches-proving-vendored-dependencies"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Patch files at <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pr"
       & "e"">&lt;target&gt;/.adacovex/patches/</span></code> exist so vendored code yo"
       & "u"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cannot modify still counts toward the audit. Their best-known job is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "overlaying <strong>docstrings</strong> for strict-mode coverage. A patch can"
       & " also carry"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<strong>SPARK proof aspects</strong> so vendored dependencies participate in"
       & " the proof"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with real contracts "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " without forking or touching their sources.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""why-proof-patches-are-necessary"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>Why proof patches are necessary<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#why-proof-pa"
       & "tches-are-necessary"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Three facts force the design:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol class=""arabic simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Strict mode counts vendored code.</strong> By default adacove"
       & "x scans every"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "directory except the always-excluded ones. The excluded directories are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.git</span></co"
       & "de>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">obj</span>"
       & "</code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">tests<"
       & "/span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">"
       & "config</span></code>, and <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span c"
       & "lass=""pre"">.adacovex</span></code>. A vendored dependency"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "missing docstrings and missing contracts count against the target."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--relaxed</span"
       & "></code> skips vendored dirs but drops the audit to a quick pass "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " not"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "an option for a compliance assessment.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>gnatprove analyses a body only when the body itself opts in.<"
       & "/strong> (The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rule from <a class=""reference internal"" href=""#writing-proofs-spark-contract"
       & "s"">Writing proofs</a> above.) A"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "vendored spec with no contracts contributes nothing to the proof. A"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "vendored body without <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class"
       & "=""pre"">SPARK_Mode</span></code> is skipped entirely.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>The vendored sources are immutable.</strong> The dependency s"
       & "hips as-is. You"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cannot add contracts to it. Re-publishing a patched fork defeats the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "point of vendoring.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A proof patch is the merge of these three constraints. It re-declares the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "vendored spec with contracts (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><sp"
       & "an class=""pre"">.ads</span></code> patch). It opts the vendored body into"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the proof (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.adb"
       & "</span></code> patch). The <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span "
       & "class=""pre"">prove</span></code> subcommand merges both into a patched"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tree copy before running gnatprove "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the originals are never touched.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""how-proof-patches-are-applied"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>How proof patches are applied<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#how-proof-patc"
       & "hes-are-applied"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol class=""arabic simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Count_Pr"
       & "oof_Patches</span></code> scans <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><"
       & "span class=""pre"">&lt;target&gt;/.adacovex/patches/</span></code> for <code c"
       & "lass=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.ads</span></code> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.adb</span></co"
       & "de> files. A patch carrying any of <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"
       & """><span class=""pre"">SPARK_Mode</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal "
       & "notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Pre</span> <span class=""pre"">=&gt;</span></co"
       & "de>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Post</span"
       & "> <span class=""pre"">=&gt;</span></code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "or <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Global</span"
       & "> <span class=""pre"">=&gt;</span></code> is a <em>proof patch</em>. A docstri"
       & "ng-only patch never engages"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the proof machinery. A target with no proof patches is proved against its"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "own tree exactly as before.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Build_Pa"
       & "tched_Copy</span></code> copies the target tree (excluding <code class=""docu"
       & "tils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.git</span></code>, <code class="
       & """docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">obj</span></code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.adacovex</"
       & "span></code>) into <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""p"
       & "re"">&lt;target&gt;/obj/adacovex-proof/</span></code> and overwrites each"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proof-patched source with its merged form.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>gnatprove runs against the copy"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s root project and the resulting"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">gnatprove.out</"
       & "span></code> is copied back to <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><s"
       & "pan class=""pre"">&lt;target&gt;/obj/gnatprove/gnatprove.out</span></code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "for the assessment pipeline.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>Patch contents are folded into the prove result-cache key, so a patch"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "edit invalidates the cached proof and forces a re-prove (<code class=""docuti"
       & "ls literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--force</span></code> also"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bypasses the cache).</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The patched copy lives under the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">obj/</span></"
       & "code>, so it is excluded from"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scanning, manifest graphs, and the prove input hash.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""writing-a-spec-patch-ads"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>Writing a spec patch (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span c"
       & "lass=""pre"">.ads</span></code>)<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#writing-a-spec-pa"
       & "tch-ads"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A spec patch mirrors the vendored spec: same package name, same subprogra"
       & "m"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declarations (with docstrings, since strict mode requires them), plus the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "aspects you want gnatprove to prove:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""highlight-ada notranslate""><div class=""highlight""><pre><span></s"
       & "pan><span class=""c1"">--  .adacovex/patches/demo/deps/vt100/vt100.ads</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""kd"">package</span> <span class=""nc"">VT100</span> <span class=""n"
       & "c"">with</span> <span class=""nc"">SPARK_Mode</span> <span class=""p"">=&gt;</spa"
       & "n> <span class=""nc"">On</span> <span class=""kr"">is</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   <span class=""c1"">--  Scroll a region of the screen up.</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   <span class=""c1"">--  @param From  Starting line of scroll region.</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   <span class=""c1"">--  @param To    Ending line of scroll region.</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   <span class=""kd"">procedure</span> <span class=""nf"">Scroll_Screen</span> <"
       & "span class=""p"">(</span><span class=""nv"">From</span> <span class=""p"">: </span"
       & "><span class=""nv"">in</span> <span class=""nv"">Natural</span><span class=""p"">;"
       & "</span> <span class=""nv"">To</span> <span class=""p"">: </span><span class=""nv"""
       & ">in</span> <span class=""nv"">Natural</span><span class=""p"">)</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "     <span class=""kn"">with</span> <span class=""n"">Pre</span> <span class=""p"""
       & ">=&gt;</span> <span class=""n"">From</span> <span class=""o"">&lt;=</span> <span"
       & " class=""n"">To</span><span class=""p"">;</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""kr"">end</span> <span class=""nf"">VT100</span><span class=""p"">;</"
       & "span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</pre></div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The merge splices the package-level aspect onto the original package"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "declaration line and replaces each aspect-carrying subprogram declaration"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with the patch"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s declaration block. Subprograms the patch does not re-declare"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "with aspects are left untouched, so a patch can add a contract to one"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "subprogram without disturbing its siblings.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""writing-a-body-patch-adb"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>Writing a body patch (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span c"
       & "lass=""pre"">.adb</span></code>)<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#writing-a-body-pa"
       & "tch-adb"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The spec patch declares the contracts. The <strong>body patch</strong> is"
       & " what makes"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gnatprove actually analyse the vendored body (the body-must-opt-in rule). It"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "lives at the body"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s relative path and mirrors the body"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s declarations with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<em>stub bodies</em> that the merge ignores "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the original implementation is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "preserved:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""highlight-ada notranslate""><div class=""highlight""><pre><span></s"
       & "pan><span class=""c1"">--  .adacovex/patches/demo/deps/vecmath/vecmath.adb</sp"
       & "an>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""kd"">package</span> <span class=""kd"">body</span> <span class=""nc"
       & """>Vecmath</span> <span class=""nc"">with</span> <span class=""nc"">SPARK_Mode</s"
       & "pan> <span class=""p"">=&gt;</span> <span class=""nc"">On</span> <span class=""kr"
       & """>is</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   <span class=""kd"">function</span> <span class=""nf"">Clamp</span> <span clas"
       & "s=""p"">(</span><span class=""nv"">Value</span> <span class=""p"">: </span><span c"
       & "lass=""nv"">in</span> <span class=""nv"">Integer</span><span class=""p"">;</span> "
       & "<span class=""nv"">Lo</span> <span class=""p"">: </span><span class=""nv"">in</spa"
       & "n> <span class=""nv"">Integer</span><span class=""p"">;</span> <span class=""nv"">"
       & "Hi</span> <span class=""p"">: </span><span class=""nv"">in</span> <span class=""n"
       & "v"">Integer</span><span class=""p"">)</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "     <span class=""kr"">return</span> <span class=""kt"">Integer</span> <span cl"
       & "ass=""kn"">with</span> <span class=""n"">SPARK_Mode</span> <span class=""p"">=&gt;"
       & "</span> <span class=""n"">On</span> <span class=""kr"">is</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   <span class=""kr"">begin</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "      <span class=""kc"">null</span><span class=""p"">;</span>  <span class=""c1"""
       & ">--  stub: the original body's implementation is kept</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   <span class=""kr"">end</span> <span class=""nf"">Clamp</span><span class=""p"">"
       & ";</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""kr"">end</span> <span class=""nf"">Vecmath</span><span class=""p"">;"
       & "</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</pre></div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The merge replaces the original declaration (up to its <code class=""docut"
       & "ils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">is</span></code>) with the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "patch"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s aspect-carrying declaration and keeps the original body proper, so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the copy gnatprove sees is <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span "
       & "class=""pre"">package</span> <span class=""pre"">body</span> <span class=""pre"">V"
       & "ecmath</span> <span class=""pre"">with</span> <span class=""pre"">SPARK_Mode</sp"
       & "an> <span class=""pre"">=&gt;</span> <span class=""pre"">On</span> <span class="""
       & "pre"">is</span> <span class=""pre"">...</span> <span class=""pre"">&lt;original</"
       & "span> <span class=""pre"">implementation&gt;</span> <span class=""pre"">...</spa"
       & "n></code>. A fully SPARK-clean body needs only the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "package-level aspect. The per-subprogram aspect covers bodies with a mix of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "clean and I/O-bound subprograms.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""matching-rules"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>Matching rules<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#matching-rules"" title=""Link t"
       & "o this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The merge matches each patched declaration against the original by <stron"
       & "g>name and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "normalised parameter profile</strong>:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>Matching is whitespace-insensitive. A single-line parameter list matc"
       & "hes a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "multi-line one.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>The default <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""p"
       & "re"">in</span></code> mode is equivalent to a bare mode (<code class=""docutil"
       & "s literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">X</span> <span class=""pre"">:</span>"
       & " <span class=""pre"">in</span> <span class=""pre"">Integer</span></code> matches"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">X</span> <span "
       & "class=""pre"">:</span> <span class=""pre"">Integer</span></code>). <code class="""
       & "docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">in</span> <span class=""pre"">"
       & "out</span></code> and <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class"
       & "=""pre"">out</span></code> are distinct modes.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>an overloaded subprogram patches its exact signature "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a patched"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "two-argument <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Sc"
       & "roll_Screen</span></code> replaces the two-argument original, never a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "same-named sibling;</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>a spec declaration terminates at its <code class=""docutils literal no"
       & "translate""><span class=""pre"">;</span></code>, a body declaration at its <cod"
       & "e class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">is</span></code>;</"
       & "p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>a patched subprogram with <strong>no match</strong> in the original f"
       & "ails loudly (the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "patch is skipped and reported) rather than silently dropping the contract.</"
       & "p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""worked-example-vecmath-clamp"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>Worked example: <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class="""
       & "pre"">Vecmath.Clamp</span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#worked-example-"
       & "vecmath-clamp"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A vendored package whose spec and body carry no contracts:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""highlight-ada notranslate""><div class=""highlight""><pre><span></s"
       & "pan><span class=""c1"">--  demo/deps/vecmath/vecmath.ads (vendored, unmodified"
       & ")</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""kd"">package</span> <span class=""nc"">Vecmath</span> <span class="
       & """kr"">is</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   <span class=""kd"">function</span> <span class=""nf"">Clamp</span> <span clas"
       & "s=""p"">(</span><span class=""nv"">Value</span> <span class=""p"">: </span><span c"
       & "lass=""nv"">in</span> <span class=""nv"">Integer</span><span class=""p"">;</span> "
       & "<span class=""nv"">Lo</span> <span class=""p"">: </span><span class=""nv"">in</spa"
       & "n> <span class=""nv"">Integer</span><span class=""p"">;</span> <span class=""nv"">"
       & "Hi</span> <span class=""p"">: </span><span class=""nv"">in</span> <span class=""n"
       & "v"">Integer</span><span class=""p"">)</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "     <span class=""kr"">return</span> <span class=""kt"">Integer</span><span cla"
       & "ss=""p"">;</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""kr"">end</span> <span class=""nf"">Vecmath</span><span class=""p"">;"
       & "</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</pre></div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""highlight-ada notranslate""><div class=""highlight""><pre><span></s"
       & "pan><span class=""c1"">--  demo/deps/vecmath/vecmath.adb (vendored, unmodified"
       & ")</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""kd"">package</span> <span class=""kd"">body</span> <span class=""nc"
       & """>Vecmath</span> <span class=""kr"">is</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   <span class=""kd"">function</span> <span class=""nf"">Clamp</span> <span clas"
       & "s=""p"">(</span><span class=""nv"">Value</span> <span class=""p"">: </span><span c"
       & "lass=""nv"">in</span> <span class=""nv"">Integer</span><span class=""p"">;</span> "
       & "<span class=""nv"">Lo</span> <span class=""p"">: </span><span class=""nv"">in</spa"
       & "n> <span class=""nv"">Integer</span><span class=""p"">;</span> <span class=""nv"">"
       & "Hi</span> <span class=""p"">: </span><span class=""nv"">in</span> <span class=""n"
       & "v"">Integer</span><span class=""p"">)</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "     <span class=""kr"">return</span> <span class=""kt"">Integer</span> <span cl"
       & "ass=""kr"">is</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   <span class=""kr"">begin</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "      <span class=""kr"">if</span> <span class=""n"">Value</span> <span class=""o"
       & """>&lt;</span> <span class=""n"">Lo</span> <span class=""kr"">then</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "         <span class=""kr"">return</span> <span class=""n"">Lo</span><span class"
       & "=""p"">;</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "      <span class=""kr"">elsif</span> <span class=""n"">Value</span> <span class"
       & "=""o"">&gt;</span> <span class=""n"">Hi</span> <span class=""kr"">then</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "         <span class=""kr"">return</span> <span class=""n"">Hi</span><span class"
       & "=""p"">;</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "      <span class=""kr"">else</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "         <span class=""kr"">return</span> <span class=""n"">Value</span><span cl"
       & "ass=""p"">;</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "      <span class=""kr"">end</span> <span class=""kr"">if</span><span class=""p"">"
       & ";</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "   <span class=""kr"">end</span> <span class=""nf"">Clamp</span><span class=""p"">"
       & ";</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""kr"">end</span> <span class=""nf"">Vecmath</span><span class=""p"">;"
       & "</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</pre></div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The two patch files from above (spec with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Pre</span> <spa"
       & "n class=""pre"">=&gt;</span> <span class=""pre"">Lo</span> <span class=""pre"">&lt"
       & ";=</span> <span class=""pre"">Hi,</span> <span class=""pre"">Post</span> <span c"
       & "lass=""pre"">=&gt;</span> <span class=""pre"">Clamp'Result</span> <span class=""p"
       & "re"">in</span> <span class=""pre"">Lo</span> <span class=""pre"">..</span> <span "
       & "class=""pre"">Hi</span></code>, and body with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">SPARK_Mode</spa"
       & "n> <span class=""pre"">=&gt;</span> <span class=""pre"">On</span></code>) merge "
       & "into the copy unchanged in behaviour. gnatprove"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proves the contract: 2 VCs (the <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><"
       & "span class=""pre"">Clamp</span></code> postcondition and its termination"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "check), 0 unproved. A caller in the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s own code can then rely on the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "contract without the vendored sources ever changing.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""when-contracts-prove-and-when-they-are-skipped"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>When contracts prove "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " and when they are skipped<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#when-contracts-prove-"
       & "and-when-they-are-skipped"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>SPARK-clean body + body patch</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " gnatprove proves the patched"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "contracts outright (the example above).</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>I/O-bound body</strong> (calls <code class=""docutils literal "
       & "notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Ada.Text_IO</span></code>, which is <code cla"
       & "ss=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">SPARK_Mode</span> <span "
       & "class=""pre"">Off</span></code>) "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & ASCII.LF
       & "gnatprove skips the I/O bodies by design and reports the unit out of proof"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scope. The contracts are still <em>declared</em> and the mechanism is exerci"
       & "sed,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "but the body is not proved "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " and crucially, it never drags the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proof level down. This is the VT100 dogfood case in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a class=""reference external"" href=""https://github.com/bladeacer/Ada_CRDT"">A"
       & "da_CRDT</a>.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""common-pitfalls"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>Common pitfalls<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#common-pitfalls"" title=""Link"
       & " to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Spec patch without a body patch.</strong> A SPARK-clean vendo"
       & "red body stays out"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "of proof scope. gnatprove reports "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "no checks generated"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " or skips the unit."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Add the <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.adb</s"
       & "pan></code> patch to opt the body in.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>A patched declaration that does not match anything.</strong> "
       & "Check the name and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the parameter list (modes included) against the original. The merge reports"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">could</span> <s"
       & "pan class=""pre"">not</span> <span class=""pre"">be</span> <span class=""pre"">mer"
       & "ged</span> <span class=""pre"">...</span> <span class=""pre"">(unmatched</span> "
       & "<span class=""pre"">subprogram</span> <span class=""pre"">or</span> <span class="
       & """pre"">oversized</span> <span class=""pre"">file)</span></code> and skips"
