       & ASCII.LF
       & "        <article role=""main"" id=""furo-main-content"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "          <section id=""ste100-technical-names-for-adacovex"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h1>STE100 Technical Names for adacovex<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#ste100-t"
       & "echnical-names-for-adacovex"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English (Section 1, "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Words"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ") defines a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "controlled vocabulary. Most words in that vocabulary are standard STE words."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Some concepts have no accurate standard STE word. For those concepts, the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "project approves a <strong>Technical Name (TN)</strong>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A Technical Name is a non-STE word that the project explicitly approves. "
       & "The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "project approves it because no standard STE word describes the concept with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the same precision. A TN has a single mandatory part of speech and a defined"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scope. The scope is restricted to the software domain of adacovex.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>This page is the controlled list of Technical Names for adacovex. Writers"
       & " of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "user documentation, API documentation, docstrings, and changelogs must use"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "these terms as defined here. If you need a term that is not in this list,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "add it to the list first, then use it.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""categories-for-ada-technical-names"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Categories for Ada Technical Names<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#categorie"
       & "s-for-ada-technical-names"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Group the Technical Names by their structural role in the software domain"
       & ".</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Hardware and System Entities.</strong> Physical components, b"
       & "uses, or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "microarchitectures that the Ada code interacts with. For example, CPU core.<"
       & "/p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Ada Language Constructs.</strong> Specific language features "
       & "that generic"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "English words cannot replace without losing technical precision. For"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "example, pragma, discriminant, rendezvous, task.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Domain and Mathematical Terms.</strong> Algorithmic, mathemat"
       & "ical, or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "mission-specific logic terms. For example, telemetry, checksum,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "quaternion.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Code Identifier Names.</strong> Exact package, type, subtype,"
       & " subprogram, and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "variable names as declared in the source code. For example,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">System.Storage_"
       & "Elements</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span cla"
       & "ss=""pre"">Buffer_Size</span></code>. This category also covers exact"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "file names, tool commands, and flag names that appear in documentation.</p><"
       & "/li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""required-data-fields-for-each-entry"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Required data fields for each entry<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#required"
       & "-data-fields-for-each-entry"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>ASD-STE100 requires strict controls over how approved words are documente"
       & "d."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Every Technical Name in this dictionary has all five fields:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper colwidths-auto docutils container"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table class=""docutils align-default"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><th class=""head""><p>Field</p></th>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<th class=""head""><p>Description</p></th>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<th class=""head""><p>Example</p></th>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-even""><td><p><strong>Approved Word (TN)</strong></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>The exact word or identifier.</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p><strong>Pragma</strong></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><td><p><strong>Part of Speech</strong></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>STE permits a word as only <em>one</em> part of speech (Noun, Verb, M"
       & "odifier).</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Noun</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-even""><td><p><strong>Approved Meaning / Definition</strong></"
       & "p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Clear, unambiguous definition restricted to the adacovex domain.</p><"
       & "/td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>A compiler directive in the Ada programming language.</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><td><p><strong>Non-Approved Alternatives</strong></p></t"
       & "d>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Terms that authors must NOT use instead of this TN.</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p><em>Compiler directive</em>, <em>Annotation</em></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-even""><td><p><strong>Example Sentence</strong></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>A compliant STE sentence demonstrating usage.</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p><em>Add the <strong>pragma</strong> to the top of the package specifi"
       & "cation.</em></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""key-rules-for-ada-technical-names"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Key rules for Ada Technical Names<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#key-rules-"
       & "for-ada-technical-names"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Nouns stay nouns.</strong> Technical Names are almost always "
       & "approved as Nouns"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "or Modifiers. Never approve a code action as a verb if a standard STE verb"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "exists. For example, use the approved verb <em>Calculate</em> instead of cre"
       & "ating"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "a TN verb <em>Compute</em>.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Exact case matching.</strong> Treat Ada identifiers (<code cl"
       & "ass=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Pascal_Case</span></cod"
       & "e> or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">UPPER_CASE</spa"
       & "n></code>) as literal Technical Names. Use the exact casing in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "documentation. This rule distinguishes language concepts from code"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "entities.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>No synonyms.</strong> If the project approves <em>Task</em> a"
       & "s a TN for an Ada"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "concurrent execution unit, do not use words like <em>Thread</em>, <em>Proces"
       & "s</em>, or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<em>Job</em> for that concept.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>One part of speech per word.</strong> A TN is a Noun or a Mod"
       & "ifier, never both."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "When you need the action, use the standard STE verb that matches the noun"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "form.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""standard-entry-template"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Standard entry template<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#standard-entry-templ"
       & "ate"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""highlight-markdown notranslate""><div class=""highlight""><pre><spa"
       & "n></span><span class=""gu"">### Technical Name: Task</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""k"">-</span><span class=""w""> </span><span class=""gs"">**Part of S"
       & "peech:**</span> Noun"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""k"">-</span><span class=""w""> </span><span class=""gs"">**Category:"
       & "**</span> Ada Language Construct"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""k"">-</span><span class=""w""> </span><span class=""gs"">**Definitio"
       & "n:**</span> A standalone unit of concurrent execution in Ada."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""k"">-</span><span class=""w""> </span><span class=""gs"">**Approved "
       & "Form:**</span> Task (singular), Tasks (plural)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""k"">-</span><span class=""w""> </span><span class=""gs"">**Do Not Us"
       & "e:**</span> Thread, Process, Job, Execution Unit"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""k"">-</span><span class=""w""> </span><span class=""gs"">**Correct E"
       & "xample:**</span> <span class=""ge"">*The main **task*</span>* waits for the se"
       & "nsor <span class=""gs"">**task**</span> to finish.*"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""k"">-</span><span class=""w""> </span><span class=""gs"">**Incorrect"
       & " Example:**</span> <span class=""ge"">*The main process waits for the sensor t"
       & "hread to complete.*</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</pre></div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""dictionary"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Dictionary<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#dictionary"" title=""Link to this h"
       & "eading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""category-ada-language-constructs"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>Category: Ada Language Constructs<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#category-a"
       & "da-language-constructs"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""technical-name-package"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4>Technical Name: Package<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#technical-name-packa"
       & "ge"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h4>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Part of Speech:</strong> Noun</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Definition:</strong> A named collection of related declaratio"
       & "ns in Ada. A"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "package has a visible specification and a private body.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Approved Form:</strong> Package (singular), Packages (plural)"
       & "</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Do Not Use:</strong> Module, Library unit, Component</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Correct Example:</strong> <em>A <strong>package</strong> grou"
       & "ps the related subprograms.</em></p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Incorrect Example:</strong> <em>A module groups the related s"
       & "ubprograms.</em></p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""technical-name-package-body"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h4>Technical Name: Package Body<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#technical-name-"
       & "package-body"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
