       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""flag-details"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Flag details<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#flag-details"" title=""Link to th"
       & "is heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""target-path"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--target=PA"
       & "TH</span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#target-path"" title=""Link to thi"
       & "s heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Project to analyse. Relative paths are resolved against the current worki"
       & "ng"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "directory to an absolute path. The path determines the root directory for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "source scanning, manifest detection, SVG badge output, and patch file"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "resolution. Default: the current working directory.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""manifest-path"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--manifest="
       & "PATH</span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#manifest-path"" title=""Link to"
       & " this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Override the project manifest file. Auto-detected from"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">&lt;target&gt;/"
       & "alire-dev.toml</span></code> or <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><"
       & "span class=""pre"">&lt;target&gt;/alire.toml</span></code> (dev first). The ma"
       & "nifest"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "path is shown in stderr output and used by <code class=""docutils literal not"
       & "ranslate""><span class=""pre"">adacovex</span> <span class=""pre"">sbom</span></c"
       & "ode> to resolve the root"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "project metadata for the dependency graph.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""dal-level"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--dal=LEVEL"
       & "</span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#dal-level"" title=""Link to this he"
       & "ading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>DO-178C DAL level (and the shared rigour tier): <code class=""docutils lit"
       & "eral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">A</span></code>, <code class=""docutils l"
       & "iteral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">B</span></code>, <code class=""docutils"
       & " literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">C</span></code>, <code class=""docuti"
       & "ls literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">D</span></code>, or <code class=""d"
       & "ocutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">E</span></code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(case-insensitive). It determines the minimum SPARK proof level required and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the specific criteria checked. This tier is shared across standards."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--dal=C</span><"
       & "/code> is DAL-C under DO-178C, ASIL B under ISO 26262, and safety Class A"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "under IEC 62304. See <a class=""reference internal"" href=""../api-docs/adacove"
       & "x-dal-levels.html""><span class=""std std-doc"">DAL levels</span></a> and"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a class=""reference internal"" href=""standards.html""><span class=""std std-doc"
       & """>Standards</span></a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""asil-level"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--asil=LEVE"
       & "L</span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#asil-level"" title=""Link to this "
       & "heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>ISO 26262 Automotive Safety Integrity Level: <code class=""docutils litera"
       & "l notranslate""><span class=""pre"">A</span></code>, <code class=""docutils lite"
       & "ral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">B</span></code>, <code class=""docutils li"
       & "teral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">C</span></code>, <code class=""docutils "
       & "literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">D</span></code>, or <code class=""docu"
       & "tils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">QM</span></code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(case-insensitive). It sets the standard to <code class=""docutils literal no"
       & "translate""><span class=""pre"">iso26262</span></code> and maps the ASIL level"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "to the shared rigour tier (ASIL D -&gt; DAL A, ASIL C -&gt; DAL B, ASIL B -&"
       & "gt; DAL C,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "ASIL A -&gt; DAL D, QM -&gt; DAL E). As a result, <code class=""docutils lite"
       & "ral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--asil=B</span></code> is the clearest sp"
       & "elling"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "of "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "assess this project at ASIL B"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ". See"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a class=""reference internal"" href=""../api-docs/adacovex-asil-levels.html""><"
       & "span class=""std std-doc"">ASIL Levels</span></a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""class-level"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--class=LEV"
       & "EL</span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#class-level"" title=""Link to thi"
       & "s heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>IEC 62304 software safety class: <code class=""docutils literal notranslat"
       & "e""><span class=""pre"">A</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notransl"
       & "ate""><span class=""pre"">B</span></code>, or <code class=""docutils literal not"
       & "ranslate""><span class=""pre"">C</span></code> (case-insensitive). It sets"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the standard to <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"""
       & ">iec62304</span></code> and maps the class to the shared rigour tier"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(Class C -&gt; DAL A, Class B -&gt; DAL B, Class A -&gt; DAL C). As a result"
       & ","
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--class=A</span"
       & "></code> is the clearest spelling of "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "assess this project at safety Class"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "A"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & ". See <a class=""reference internal"" href=""../api-docs/adacovex-class-levels."
       & "html""><span class=""std std-doc"">Safety Classes</span></a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""standard-name"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--standard="
       & "NAME</span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#standard-name"" title=""Link to"
       & " this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Select the compliance standard used to label the assessment (default"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">do178c</span></"
       & "code>). The evidence checks are identical across standards. Only the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "integrity-level names change in the report and badges:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">do178c</"
       & "span></code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " DAL A"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & "E (avionics)</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">iso26262"
       & "</span></code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " ASIL D / C / B / A / QM (automotive)</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">iec62304"
       & "</span></code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " Class C / B / A / no class (medical-device software)</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">all</spa"
       & "n></code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " run one assessment at the shared tier and emit badges/reports for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "every standard (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"""
       & ">do178c.svg</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span "
       & "class=""pre"">iso26262.svg</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notran"
       & "slate""><span class=""pre"">iec62304.svg</span></code>)</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Accepted case-insensitively, with or without the hyphen/space (<code clas"
       & "s=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">ISO-26262</span></code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">iec62304</span>"
       & "</code>, and more). See <a class=""reference internal"" href=""standards.html"">"
       & "<span class=""std std-doc"">Standards</span></a> for the full tier"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "mapping.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>When both a dedicated level flag (<code class=""docutils literal notransla"
       & "te""><span class=""pre"">--asil</span></code> / <code class=""docutils literal n"
       & "otranslate""><span class=""pre"">--class</span></code>) and <code class=""docuti"
       & "ls literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--standard</span></code> are"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "passed, the dedicated flag sets the standard. <code class=""docutils literal "
       & "notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--standard</span></code> is ignored for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "labelling (last-write-wins per field). The shared tier is always whatever th"
       & "e"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "level flag (or <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">"
       & "--dal</span></code>) resolved to.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""status"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">status</spa"
       & "n></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#status"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">adacovex</sp"
       & "an> <span class=""pre"">status</span> <span class=""pre"">[--target=PATH]</span>"
       & "</code> reports toolchain and platform state. It"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "does not run an assessment. It does not download or deploy anything. It"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "reports the following:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>whether Alire is installed</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>how gnatprove is resolved</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>the host CPU count and CI status (and the resulting default <code cla"
       & "ss=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">-j</span></code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "parallelism)</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>a <strong>VCS report</strong> (which VCS tools are on <code class=""do"
       & "cutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">$PATH</span></code> and which "
       & "manages the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "target "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " see <a class=""reference internal"" href=""vcs.html""><span class=""std std-doc"""
       & ">VCS support</span></a>)</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>mandb availability</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>the effective display timezone, the current date/time in it, and how "
       & "many"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "dated release changelogs the target carries</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">adacovex</sp"
       & "an> <span class=""pre"">status</span> <span class=""pre"">--tz=ZONE</span></code"
       & "> (or <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--timezon"
       & "e=ZONE</span></code>) overrides the display"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "timezone for the report. It shows the effective timezone, the current date"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and time in that zone, and how many dated release changelogs the target"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "carries. Exit <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">0"
       & "</span></code> when a usable gnatprove is detectable without a download."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Exit <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">1</span></"
       & "code> otherwise; for full detail see"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a class=""reference internal"" href=""platforms.html#status-subcommand""><span "
       & "class=""std std-ref"">Platforms "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">status</span><"
       & "/code> subcommand</span></a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">adacovex</sp"
       & "an> <span class=""pre"">status</span> <span class=""pre"">--export</span></code>"
       & " prints the report as machine-readable JSON on"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "stdout; <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">status<"
       & "/span> <span class=""pre"">--export=PATH</span></code> writes it to <code clas"
       & "s=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">PATH</span></code>. Scrip"
       & "ts and CI can"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "consume it without parsing prose. <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"""
       & "><span class=""pre"">adacovex</span> <span class=""pre"">status</span> <span cla"
       & "ss=""pre"">--metrics</span></code> prints the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "same data as compact <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class="
       & """pre"">key=value</span></code> lines, one per line, for shell scripts."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Both flags only work with the <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><sp"
       & "an class=""pre"">status</span></code> subcommand.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""complexity"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">complexity<"
       & "/span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#complexity"" title=""Link to this he"
       & "ading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">adacovex</sp"
       & "an> <span class=""pre"">complexity</span> <span class=""pre"">[--target=PATH]</s"
       & "pan> <span class=""pre"">[--excludes=EXT,EXT]</span></code> runs a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "cyclomatic-complexity and LOC check across the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s source files in many"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "languages. <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--ex"
       & "cludes=EXT,EXT</span></code> skips comma-separated file extensions (for"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "example <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">md,rst<"
       & "/span></code>) and only works with the <code class=""docutils literal notrans"
       & "late""><span class=""pre"">complexity</span></code> subcommand. It prints"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "a tokei-style summary (files, lines, code, comments, blanks) plus a per-file"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "table of <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Lines="
       & "</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"""
       & ">Code=</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class"
       & "=""pre"">Comments=</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><"
       & "span class=""pre"">Blanks=</span></code>, the codebase loc"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "percentage, and the cyclomatic complexity <code class=""docutils literal notr"
       & "anslate""><span class=""pre"">cx=</span></code>. The gate fails when a file"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "or function exceeds the thresholds (defaults: 4 000 LOC, 10% of codebase per"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "file, 120 per function, 600 per file).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Exit <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">0</span"
       & "></code> when all gates pass. Exit <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"
       & """><span class=""pre"">1</span></code> otherwise. This replaces the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "previous Python <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"""
       & ">check-complexity.py</span></code> script. Maintainers wire the same gate"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "into their CI via <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pr"
       & "e"">adacovex</span> <span class=""pre"">complexity</span> <span class=""pre"">--e"
       & "xcludes=...</span></code>; see the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a class=""reference internal"" href=""../contributing/developer-guide.html""><s"
       & "pan class=""std std-doc"">developer guide</span></a> for the workflow.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""the-prove-subcommand"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>The <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">prove</"
       & "span></code> subcommand<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#the-prove-subcommand"" ti"
       & "tle=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">adacovex</sp"
       & "an> <span class=""pre"">prove</span> <span class=""pre"">--target=PATH</span></c"
       & "ode> resolves a gnatprove installation and runs it against the target. It th"
       & "en falls through to the normal assessment pipeline. The pipeline parses the "
       & "freshly generated proof summary. As a result, one command both proves and as"
       & "sesses.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>For the full guide to proving and writing SPARK proofs (contracts, VC cat"
       & "egories, proof patches for vendored deps), see <a class=""reference internal"""
       & " href=""../contributing/proving.html""><span class=""std std-doc"">Proving and w"
       & "riting proofs</span></a>. gnatprove is resolved in this order: manifest pin "
       & "&gt; global pin &gt; <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class="
       & """pre"">$PATH</span></code> &gt; cached toolchain &gt; download. The target do"
       & "es not need to declare gnatprove. Full detail: <a class=""reference internal"""
       & " href=""../contributing/architecture.html#gnatprove-toolchain-resolution-prov"
       & "e-subcommand""><span class=""std std-ref"">Architecture "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " GNATprove toolchain resolution</span></a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The proof summary is written to <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"
       & """><span class=""pre"">&lt;target&gt;/obj/gnatprove/gnatprove.out</span></code>"
       & " (the same location the assessment discovers). The SVG badges are emitted as"
       & " usual. The result cache serves unchanged targets. <code class=""docutils lit"
       & "eral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--force</span></code> bypasses the cache"
       & " and forces a full gnatprove reanalysis. When the target carries proof patch"
       & "es (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.adacovex/p"
       & "atches/</span></code>), gnatprove runs against a patched tree copy at <code "
       & "class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">&lt;target&gt;/obj/ad"
       & "acovex-proof/</span></code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Vendored dependencies then participate in the proof without their sources"
       & " being touched. See <a class=""reference internal"" href=""../contributing/prov"
       & "ing.html#proof-patches-proving-vendored-dependencies""><span class=""std std-r"
       & "ef"">Proving and writing proofs</span></a> for how to write them, and <a clas"
       & "s=""reference internal"" href=""../contributing/architecture.html#proof-patches"
       & "-spark-contracts-over-vendored-dependencies""><span class=""std std-ref"">Archi"
       & "tecture "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " Proof patches</span></a> for the design.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper colwidths-auto docutils container"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table class=""docutils align-default"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><th class=""head""><p>Flag</p></th>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<th class=""head""><p>Default</p></th>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<th class=""head""><p>Description</p></th>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-even""><td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span"
       & " class=""pre"">--jobs=N</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notransla"
       & "te""><span class=""pre"">-j</span> <span class=""pre"">N</span></code></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>auto</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>GNATprove parallelism: auto-detect (max(1, cores-2), all cores in CI)"
       & ", <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">0</span></cod"
       & "e> = all cores, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"""
       & ">N</span></code> = pin N processes</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span "
       & "class=""pre"">--level=N</span></code></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>tool default</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>GNATprove proof effort, 0-4</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-even""><td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span"
       & " class=""pre"">--timeout=N</span></code></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>tool default</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Per-check prover timeout in seconds</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span "
       & "class=""pre"">--steps=N</span></code></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">10000</s"
       & "pan></code></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Max proof steps (reproducible budget, an explicit value overrides the"
       & " default)</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-even""><td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span"
       & " class=""pre"">--memlimit=N</span></code></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>tool default</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Prover memory limit in MB</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span "
       & "class=""pre"">--force</span></code></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>off</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Force full gnatprove reanalysis (<code class=""docutils literal notran"
       & "slate""><span class=""pre"">-f</span></code>). Also bypasses the result cache</"
       & "p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-even""><td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span"
       & " class=""pre"">--no-loop-unrolling</span></code></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>always on</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Disable automatic loop unrolling. Loop unrolling is always disabled, "
       & "so GNATprove never emits the purely-informational <code class=""docutils lite"
       & "ral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">cannot</span> <span class=""pre"">unroll</s"
       & "pan> <span class=""pre"">loop</span> <span class=""pre"">(too</span> <span class"
       & "=""pre"">many</span> <span class=""pre"">loop</span> <span class=""pre"">iteration"
       & "s)</span> <span class=""pre"">[info-unrolling-inlining]</span></code> notice. "
       & "It is proof-neutral for the dogfood targets (720/720 adacovex, 589/589 Ada_C"
       & "RDT VCs, 0 unproved). Flag kept for compatibility</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span "
       & "class=""pre"">--no-inlining</span></code></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>off</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Disable contextual analysis inlining</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-even""><td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span"
       & " class=""pre"">--quiet</span></code></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>on</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Hide GNATprove"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s benign info messages (the default suppression set, the loop-unrolling/inli"
       & "ning notice blocks) from stdout. It is active by default for local runs. <co"
       & "de class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--verbose</span></"
       & "code> always shows every message and wins over it. CI passes <code class=""do"
       & "cutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--verbose</span></code>, so CI"
       & " output stays authoritative. This is the explicit form of the default</p></t"
       & "d>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span "
       & "class=""pre"">--suppress-warnings</span></code></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>on</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Alias of <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"""
       & ">--quiet</span></code> (the default suppression set). Kept for compatibility"
       & "</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-even""><td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span"
       & " class=""pre"">--suppress-warnings=SETS</span></code></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>on</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Hide GNATprove info messages whose tags match the comma-separated sup"
       & "pression-set names (for example <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><"
       & "span class=""pre"">--suppress-warnings=unrolling-inlining,xyz</span></code>). "
       & "A set name <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">S</s"
       & "pan></code> suppresses blocks tagged <code class=""docutils literal notransla"
       & "te""><span class=""pre"">[info-S]</span></code> (or bare <code class=""docutils "
       & "literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">[S]</span></code>). <code class=""docu"
       & "tils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--verbose</span></code> always s"
       & "hows every message</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">prove</span>"
       & "</code> accepts all assessment flags too (<code class=""docutils literal notr"
       & "anslate""><span class=""pre"">--dal</span></code>, <code class=""docutils litera"
       & "l notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--standard</span></code>, the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--require-*</sp"
       & "an></code> gates, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pr"
       & "e"">--emit-svg</span></code>, and more), so CI gates apply to the proof"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "run directly. <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">-"
       & "-force</span></code> is shared with <code class=""docutils literal notranslat"
       & "e""><span class=""pre"">man</span> <span class=""pre"">--force</span></code> (see"
       & " below). The"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "remaining prove flags are validated only in prove mode.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""automatic-sbom-no-sbom-sbom-format"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>Automatic SBOM (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class="""
       & "pre"">--no-sbom</span></code> / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><s"
       & "pan class=""pre"">--sbom-format</span></code>)<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#aut"
       & "omatic-sbom-no-sbom-sbom-format"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Every assessment writes a proof-aware SBOM by default (the pipeline"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s last"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "step): <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">&lt;targ"
       & "et&gt;/sbom.json</span></code> (CycloneDX 1.5), <code class=""docutils litera"
       & "l notranslate""><span class=""pre"">&lt;target&gt;/sbom.spdx.json</span></code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(SPDX 2.3), or <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">"
       & "&lt;target&gt;/docs/compliance/SBOM.md</span></code> depending on"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--sbom-format</"
       & "span></code> (default <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class"
       & "=""pre"">cyclonedx-json</span></code>). <code class=""docutils literal notransl"
       & "ate""><span class=""pre"">--no-sbom</span></code> skips it entirely."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "These are separate from the dedicated <a class=""reference internal"" href=""sb"
       & "om.html""><span class=""std std-doc""><code class=""docutils literal notranslate"
       & """><span class=""pre"">sbom</span></code> subcommand</span></a>, which"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "writes a single SBOM at an explicit path and exits.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""serve"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--serve</sp"
       & "an></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#serve"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A <strong>switch</strong>: when given, adacovex scans and assesses the ta"
       & "rget, then starts the built-in HTTP/1.1 web dashboard on <code class=""docuti"
       & "ls literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--port</span></code> (default <cod"
       & "e class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">8080</span></code>)"
       & " and blocks until interrupted. Passing <code class=""docutils literal notrans"
       & "late""><span class=""pre"">--serve</span></code> is the only way to start the s"
       & "erver; omitting it (the default, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"">"
       & "<span class=""pre"">off</span></code>) renders and exits without serving. Ther"
       & "e is no <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--no-se"
       & "rve</span></code>, because the flag already controls it. It serves an HTML d"
       & "ashboard at <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">/</"
       & "span></code>, a JSON API at <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span"
       & " class=""pre"">/api/metrics</span></code>, the SVG badges at <code class=""docu"
       & "tils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">/badge/*.svg</span></code>, and "
       & "the bundled offline manual at <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><sp"
       & "an class=""pre"">/docs</span></code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The dashboard is standard-aware (it defaults to all standards) and suppor"
       & "ts light, dark, and system themes.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Full detail, the JSON schema, the theme-resolution order, and embedding t"
       & "ips are in <a class=""reference internal"" href=""dashboard.html""><span class="""
       & "std std-doc"">Web dashboard and JSON API</span></a>. Related flags: <code cla"
       & "ss=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--port</span></code>, <c"
       & "ode class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--serve-workers</"
       & "span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">-"
       & "-theme</span></code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""theme-name"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--theme=NAM"
       & "E</span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#theme-name"" title=""Link to this "
       & "heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Dashboard colour theme for <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><sp"
       & "an class=""pre"">--serve</span></code>: <code class=""docutils literal notransl"
       & "ate""><span class=""pre"">system</span></code> (default, follows <code class=""d"
       & "ocutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">prefers-color-scheme</span></"
       & "code>), <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">light</"
       & "span></code>, or <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"
       & """>dark</span></code> (case-insensitive). It sets the initial dropdown select"
       & "ion in the served page. The header dropdown can switch live afterwards, and "
       & "<strong>Save settings</strong> persists the choice in <code class=""docutils "
       & "literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">localStorage</span></code> (no cookie"
       & "s). Only relevant with <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span clas"
       & "s=""pre"">--serve</span></code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>See <a class=""reference internal"" href=""dashboard.html#themes""><span clas"
       & "s=""std std-ref"">dashboard themes</span></a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""port-n"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--port=N</s"
       & "pan></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#port-n"" title=""Link to this heading"""
       & ">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HTTP server port when <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span cl"
       & "ass=""pre"">--serve</span></code> is used. Must be a valid <code class=""docuti"
       & "ls literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Positive</span></code> integer."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Only relevant with <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""p"
       & "re"">--serve</span></code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""serve-workers-n"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--serve-wor"
       & "kers=N</span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#serve-workers-n"" title=""Lin"
       & "k to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>HTTP server task-pool worker count when <code class=""docutils literal not"
       & "ranslate""><span class=""pre"">--serve</span></code> is used. Default is <code "
       & "class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">4</span></code>."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Raise it to handle more concurrent dashboard requests, or lower it to use"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "less memory. It must be a valid <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><"
       & "span class=""pre"">Positive</span></code> integer and only works with"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--serve</span><"
       & "/code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""tz-zone-timezone-zone"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--tz=ZONE</"
       & "span></code> / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">"
       & "--timezone=ZONE</span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#tz-zone-timezone-z"
       & "one"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Display timezone for the status report.  Accepts a well-known IANA name"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(for example <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">As"
       & "ia/Singapore</span></code>) or a fixed UTC/GMT offset (<code class=""docutils"
       & " literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">UTC+8</span></code>, <code class=""do"
       & "cutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">GMT+8</span></code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">UTC+08</span></"
       & "code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">GMT+08</"
       & "span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">U"
       & "TC+08:30</span></code>).  Without it adacovex uses the operating"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "system"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s timezone.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A named zone resolves from a built-in table of common IANA names.  A zone"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "that may observe daylight saving time, or one the table lacks, is probed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "against the platform tzdata (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><spa"
       & "n class=""pre"">zdump</span></code> + <code class=""docutils literal notranslat"
       & "e""><span class=""pre"">date</span> <span class=""pre"">+%z</span></code>) for th"
       & "e DST-correct"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "current offset, with the table as the fallback when the probe is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "unavailable.  Values are matched case-insensitively, and a bad value fails"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "loudly.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""emit-svg-path"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--emit-svg="
       & "PATH</span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#emit-svg-path"" title=""Link to"
       & " this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Write SVG badges to a directory. Default <code class=""docutils literal no"
       & "translate""><span class=""pre"">&lt;target&gt;/docs/badges</span></code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(project-scoped). Creates:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">spark.sv"
       & "g</span></code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " SPARK assurance level (Stone through Platinum)</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">tests.sv"
       & "g</span></code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " test pass/fail count</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">do178c.s"
       & "vg</span></code> / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""p"
       & "re"">iso26262.svg</span></code> / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"">"
       & "<span class=""pre"">iec62304.svg</span></code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " compliance status for the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "selected standard (Achieved / Unmet), or all three with <code class=""docutil"
       & "s literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--standard=all</span></code></p></l"
       & "i>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">docs.svg"
       & "</span></code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " docstring coverage percentage</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--no-svg</sp"
       & "an></code> overrides and disables SVG output entirely.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""no-svg"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--no-svg</s"
       & "pan></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#no-svg"" title=""Link to this heading"""
       & ">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Suppress all SVG badge output. Overrides <code class=""docutils literal no"
       & "translate""><span class=""pre"">--emit-svg</span></code> if both are given.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""emit-metrics-path"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--emit-metr"
       & "ics=PATH</span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#emit-metrics-path"" title="
       & """Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>After the assessment, it writes a machine-readable JSON export to <code c"
       & "lass=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">PATH</span></code>:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">{&quot;metrics&"
       & "quot;:</span> <span class=""pre"">{...},</span> <span class=""pre"">&quot;depend"
       & "encies&quot;:</span> <span class=""pre"">{...}}</span></code>.  <code class=""d"
       & "ocutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">metrics</span></code> is the "
       & "same"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "object the dashboard JSON API serves at <code class=""docutils literal notran"
       & "slate""><span class=""pre"">/api/metrics</span></code>.  <code class=""docutils "
       & "literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">dependencies</span></code> is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the resolved dependency graph (name, version, scope, parent, purl, kind) at"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">/api/deps</span"
       & "></code>.  It is useful for scripting gates, external dashboards, or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "archiving assessment results. The composite GitHub Action uploads it as a CI"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "artifact when <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">e"
       & "mit-metrics</span></code> is set.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""emit-markdown-path"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--emit-mark"
       & "down=PATH</span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#emit-markdown-path"" titl"
       & "e=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Write compliance reports to a directory. Creates two files:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">VERIFICA"
       & "TION.md</span></code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " full verification report with all metrics</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">TRACE.md"
       & "</span></code> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " HLR traceability matrix (source-to-requirement mapping)</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""skip-dir-name"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--skip-dir="
       & "NAME</span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#skip-dir-name"" title=""Link to"
       & " this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Add a directory name to the scanner"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s skip list (repeatable). Directories whose"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "simple name matches an entry are not recursed into during source scanning."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Only effective in relaxed mode. In strict mode (default) the skip list is"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "always empty.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""relaxed"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--relaxed</"
       & "span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#relaxed"" title=""Link to this headin"
       & "g"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Disable strict mode. Enables the skip list (default <code class=""docutils"
       & " literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">demo,deps,examples</span></code> plu"
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "any <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--skip-dir<"
       & "/span></code> entries) and does NOT apply <code class=""docutils literal notr"
       & "anslate""><span class=""pre"">.adacovex/patches/</span></code>. See"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a class=""reference internal"" href=""#strict-vs-relaxed-mode"">Strict vs relax"
       & "ed mode</a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""compare-base-ref"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--compare-b"
       & "ase=REF</span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#compare-base-ref"" title=""L"
       & "ink to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Differential mode: snapshot a base revision and print a side-by-side comp"
       & "arison against the current tree (packages, subprograms, docstring %, HLR tra"
       & "ced, orphan tags, SPARK level, VCs proved, tests, DAL status). Exit <code cl"
       & "ass=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">0</span></code> only if"
       & " there are no regressions AND the current DAL is Achieved. Exit <code class="
       & """docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">1</span></code> otherwise. "
       & "Works on <strong>git, Mercurial, Subversion, Fossil, and jj</strong>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Full detail and the per-VCS snapshot mechanisms are in <a class=""referenc"
       & "e internal"" href=""vcs.html""><span class=""std std-doc"">VCS support and differ"
       & "ential assessment</span></a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""coverage-delta-ref"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--coverage-"
       & "delta=REF</span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#coverage-delta-ref"" titl"
       & "e=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Lightweight docstring-coverage gate for PR-style CI checks. Scans sources"
       & " + patches + computes docstring metrics on both a base revision and the curr"
       & "ent tree (no GNATprove/tests/DAL), prints a compact coverage table plus a ma"
       & "chine-parseable <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"""
       & ">coverage_delta:</span></code> line, and cleans up the snapshot. Exit <code "
       & "class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">0</span></code> if cu"
       & "rrent docstring coverage is <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span"
       & " class=""pre"">&gt;=</span></code> the base. Exit <code class=""docutils litera"
       & "l notranslate""><span class=""pre"">1</span></code> if coverage regressed.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Mutually exclusive with <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span "
       & "class=""pre"">--compare-base</span></code>. See <a class=""reference internal"" "
       & "href=""vcs.html""><span class=""std std-doc"">VCS support and differential asses"
       & "sment</span></a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""version"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--version</"
       & "span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#version"" title=""Link to this headin"
       & "g"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Print the bundled version (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><sp"
       & "an class=""pre"">adacovex</span> <span class=""pre"">vX.</span> <span class=""pre"
       & """>Y.</span> <span class=""pre"">Z</span></code>) and exit, without scanning or"
       & " assessing. The version source depends on the <strong>installation method</s"
       & "trong> (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">ADACOVE"
       & "X_VERSION</span></code> for release builds, <code class=""docutils literal no"
       & "translate""><span class=""pre"">alire-dev.toml</span></code> for source checkou"
       & "ts, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">alire.toml<"
       & "/span></code> for dependency-managed installs).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The same constant drives the man page, the SBOM tool version, and the res"
       & "ult-cache namespace. As a result, they cannot drift. Full detail: <a class="""
       & "reference internal"" href=""installation.html#version-source-per-installation-"
       & "method""><span class=""std std-ref"">Installation "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " version source</span></a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""completion"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">completion<"
       & "/span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#completion"" title=""Link to this he"
       & "ading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">adacovex</sp"
       & "an> <span class=""pre"">completion</span> <span class=""pre"">[SHELL]</span></co"
       & "de> (also <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">adaco"
       & "vex</span> <span class=""pre"">--completion[=SHELL]</span></code>) prints"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "a static shell-completion script to stdout and exits.  <code class=""docutils"
       & " literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">SHELL</span></code> is one of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">bash</span></co"
       & "de>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">fish</span"
       & "></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">zsh</"
       & "span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">p"
       & "wsh</span></code>, when omitted it is auto-detected from"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">$SHELL</span></"
       & "code>, falling back to bash for unknown or empty shells.  Typical setup:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""highlight-bash notranslate""><div class=""highlight""><pre><span></"
       & "span><span class=""nb"">eval</span><span class=""w""> </span><span class=""s2"">""<"
       & "/span><span class=""k"">$(</span>adacovex<span class=""w""> </span>completion<sp"
       & "an class=""k"">)</span><span class=""s2"">""</span><span class=""w"">        </span"
       & "><span class=""c1""># bash (default)</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""nb"">source</span><span class=""w""> </span>&lt;<span class=""o"">(<"
       & "/span>adacovex<span class=""w""> </span>completion<span class=""w""> </span>zsh<"
       & "span class=""o"">)</span><span class=""w"">    </span><span class=""c1""># zsh</sp"
       & "an>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "adacovex<span class=""w""> </span>completion<span class=""w""> </span>fish<span "
       & "class=""w""> </span><span class=""p"">|</span><span class=""w""> </span><span clas"
       & "s=""nb"">source</span><span class=""w"">    </span><span class=""c1""># fish</span"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "adacovex<span class=""w""> </span>completion<span class=""w""> </span>pwsh<span "
       & "class=""w""> </span><span class=""p"">|</span><span class=""w""> </span>Invoke-Exp"
       & "ression<span class=""w"">   </span><span class=""c1""># PowerShell</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</pre></div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The scripts complete the subcommands and every long flag from the binary"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "own flag table, so the completion set cannot drift from the CLI. The flag"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "list embeds at generation time. Re-run <code class=""docutils literal notrans"
       & "late""><span class=""pre"">adacovex</span> <span class=""pre"">completion</span><"
       & "/code> after upgrading"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "adacovex (a shell prompt hook that regenerates on version change works well)"
       & ".</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""man"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">man</span><"
       & "/code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#man"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">man</spa"
       & "n></code> subcommand installs the adacovex man page into the <strong>local m"
       & "an"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "database</strong> (Linux/WSL, no root required) and refreshes the index with"
       & " <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">mandb</span></"
       & "code>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "when present. <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">a"
       & "dacovex</span> <span class=""pre"">man</span> <span class=""pre"">--check</span>"
       & "</code> exits 0 when the installed page matches"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the binary. It exits 1 otherwise (a shell prompt hook can auto-update as a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "result). <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--dir="
       & "PATH</span></code> overrides the install root. Full detail, exit codes,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and the prompt-hook recipe are in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a class=""reference internal"" href=""installation.html#keeping-the-man-page-i"
       & "n-sync""><span class=""std std-ref"">Installation "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " keeping the man page in sync</span></a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""vcs-support"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>VCS support<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#vcs-support"" title=""Link to this"
       & " heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>A version control system is not required for base adacovex functi"
       & "onality</strong>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(scanning, proof analysis, test parsing, compliance assessment, SBOM generat"
       & "ion, dashboards, caching). A VCS is only needed for the differential modes ("
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--compare-base<"
       & "/span></code> / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"""
       & ">--coverage-delta</span></code>). Those modes snapshot a base revision acros"
       & "s <strong>git, Mercurial, Subversion, Fossil, and jj</strong> without touchi"
       & "ng the working tree. Detection is marker-file based (<code class=""docutils l"
       & "iteral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.git</span></code> / <code class=""docu"
       & "tils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.jj</span></code> / <code class="
       & """docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.hg</span></code> / <code c"
       & "lass=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.svn</span></code> / <"
       & "code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.fslckout</span>"
       & "</code> / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">_FOSS"
       & "IL_</span></code>) with a command-probe fallback.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Full detail, the snapshot mechanism per VCS, and the Subversion/Fossil UX"
       & " notes are in <a class=""reference internal"" href=""vcs.html""><span class=""std"
       & " std-doc"">VCS support and differential assessment</span></a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""ci-threshold-gates-require"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>CI threshold gates (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span cla"
       & "ss=""pre"">--require-*</span></code>)<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#ci-threshold"
       & "-gates-require"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The four <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--r"
       & "equire-*</span></code> flags add explicit minimum-bar checks on top of the D"
       & "AL"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "criteria. They are off by default. When set, the assessment fails loudly"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(exit code <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">1</s"
       & "pan></code>, with an explicit <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><sp"
       & "an class=""pre"">CI</span> <span class=""pre"">GATE:</span></code> reason printe"
       & "d to the report) if the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "target does not meet the required level:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""highlight-bash notranslate""><div class=""highlight""><pre><span></"
       & "span>adacovex<span class=""w""> </span>--target<span class=""o"">=</span>.<span "
       & "class=""w""> </span>--require-spark<span class=""o"">=</span>Platinum<span class"
       & "=""w""> </span>--require-docstrings<span class=""o"">=</span><span class=""m"">100"
       & "</span><span class=""w""> </span><span class=""se"">\</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""w"">         </span>--require-tests<span class=""o"">=</span><span"
       & " class=""m"">1186</span><span class=""w""> </span>--require-proof<span class=""o"""
       & ">=</span><span class=""m"">100</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</pre></div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">require-"
       & "spark</span></code> compares the honest assessed SPARK level (Stone..Platinu"
       & "m).</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">require-"
       & "docstrings</span></code> and <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><spa"
       & "n class=""pre"">require-proof</span></code> take a percentage (0-100).</p></li"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">require-"
       & "tests</span></code> takes a count of passing tests.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>CI that pins a gnatprove version (manifest or global <code class=""docutil"
       & "s literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">adacovex.toml</span></code> pin)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "must set these to the values that version actually achieves. A stricter"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "prover can legitimately leave more VCs unproved. As a result, gate on the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "results of the prover you pin.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""result-caching-cache-no-cache-cache-dir-cache-max"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>Result caching (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class="""
       & "pre"">--cache</span></code> / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><spa"
       & "n class=""pre"">--no-cache</span></code> / <code class=""docutils literal notra"
       & "nslate""><span class=""pre"">--cache-dir</span></code> / <code class=""docutils "
       & "literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--cache-max</span></code>)<a class=""h"
       & "eaderlink"" href=""#result-caching-cache-no-cache-cache-dir-cache-max"" title="""
       & "Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex persists parsed analysis results on disk, so unchanged inputs ar"
       & "e not re-scanned, re-parsed, or re-proved. Every entry is keyed by a namespa"
       & "ce prefix plus the SHA-256 of the artifact(s) it was derived from. An unchan"
       & "ged manifest/lockfile/.gpr set serves the cached dependency graph. Unchanged"
       & " HLR.md/LLR.md serve the cached requirement parses. <code class=""docutils li"
       & "teral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--no-cache</span></code> bypasses it en"
       & "tirely. <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--cache"
       & "-dir</span></code> relocates it. <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"">"
       & "<span class=""pre"">--cache-max</span></code> (default <code class=""docutils l"
       & "iteral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">4096</span></code>) caps entries befor"
       & "e oldest-first eviction.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The ANSI report shows a <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span "
       & "class=""pre"">result</span> <span class=""pre"">cache:</span> <span class=""pre"">"
       & "X</span> <span class=""pre"">hit(s),</span> <span class=""pre"">Y</span> <span c"
       & "lass=""pre"">miss(es),</span> <span class=""pre"">Z</span> <span class=""pre"">evi"
       & "cted</span></code> line per run. Full design (schema namespace, eviction, ov"
       & "erflow safety, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">"
       & "--target</span></code> normalization) is in <a class=""reference internal"" hr"
       & "ef=""../contributing/architecture.html#result-caching""><span class=""std std-r"
       & "ef"">Architecture "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " Result caching</span></a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""verbose"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--verbose</"
       & "span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#verbose"" title=""Link to this headin"
       & "g"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Print pipeline step diagnostics to stderr.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""help-and-contextual-help"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--help</spa"
       & "n></code> and contextual <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span cl"
       & "ass=""pre"">help</span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#help-and-contextual"
       & "-help"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--help</span"
       & "></code> prints all options, defaults, and examples to stdout, then exits. N"
       & "o"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scanning or assessment is performed.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Contextual help</strong>: the <code class=""docutils literal notra"
       & "nslate""><span class=""pre"">help</span></code> keyword prints flag/subcommand-"
       & "specific text"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "instead of the full usage. The topic can be given in either order, with or"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "without the leading <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class="""
       & "pre"">--</span></code>:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""highlight-default notranslate""><div class=""highlight""><pre><span"
       & "></span><span class=""n"">adacovex</span> <span class=""n"">help</span> <span cl"
       & "ass=""n"">serve</span>        <span class=""c1""># or: help --serve, --serve hel"
       & "p</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""n"">adacovex</span> <span class=""n"">help</span> <span class=""n"">"
       & "standard</span>     <span class=""c1""># standard / dal / asil / class</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""n"">adacovex</span> <span class=""n"">help</span> <span class=""n"">"
       & "sbom</span>         <span class=""c1""># subcommands: sbom, prove, status, man"
       & "</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""n"">adacovex</span> <span class=""n"">help</span> <span class=""n"">"
       & "theme</span>        <span class=""c1""># every flag has a topic (port, target,"
       & " ...)</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<span class=""n"">adacovex</span> <span class=""n"">help</span>              <sp"
       & "an class=""c1""># no topic: full usage</span>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</pre></div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The topic is case-insensitive and an <code class=""docutils literal notran"
       & "slate""><span class=""pre"">=value</span></code> suffix is ignored"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">help</span> <s"
       & "pan class=""pre"">--standard=all</span></code> == <code class=""docutils litera"
       & "l notranslate""><span class=""pre"">help</span> <span class=""pre"">standard</spa"
       & "n></code>). Unknown topics print the full"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "usage with an "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Unknown topic"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " notice. Contextual help exits <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><s"
       & "pan class=""pre"">0</span></code> and never"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "scans or assesses.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""strict-vs-relaxed-mode"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Strict vs relaxed mode<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#strict-vs-relaxed-mod"
       & "e"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper colwidths-auto docutils container"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table class=""docutils align-default"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><th class=""head""><p>Aspect</p></th>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<th class=""head""><p>Strict (default)</p></th>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<th class=""head""><p>Relaxed (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><spa"
       & "n class=""pre"">--relaxed</span></code>)</p></th>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-even""><td><p>Directory exclusions</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.git</sp"
       & "an></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">obj"
       & "</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"""
       & ">tests</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class"
       & "=""pre"">config</span></code>, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><spa"
       & "n class=""pre"">.adacovex</span></code> only</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Same + <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">d"
       & "emo,deps,examples</span></code> + <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"""
       & "><span class=""pre"">--skip-dir</span></code> additions</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><td><p>Vendored code</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Scanned and counted</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Skipped</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-even""><td><p>Patch files</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Applied from <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class="""
       & "pre"">.adacovex/patches/</span></code> (docstrings always, SPARK proof aspect"
       & "s in prove mode)</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Not applied</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><td><p>Use case</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Full compliance audit</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Quick assessment of production code</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Patch files can carry more than docstrings. A patch with <code class=""doc"
       & "utils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">SPARK_Mode</span></code> /"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Pre</span></cod"
       & "e> / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Post</span"
       & "></code> / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Glob"
       & "al</span></code> aspects is a <strong>proof patch</strong> that adds SPARK"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "contracts to vendored code in prove mode (spec patches <code class=""docutils"
       & " literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.ads</span></code>, and body"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "patches <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.adb</s"
       & "pan></code> opt the vendored body into the proof). Why they exist, how"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "to write them, worked examples, and pitfalls are in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<a class=""reference internal"" href=""../contributing/proving.html#proof-patch"
       & "es-proving-vendored-dependencies""><span class=""std std-ref"">Proving and writ"
       & "ing proofs "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " proof patches</span></a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""exit-codes"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Exit codes<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#exit-codes"" title=""Link to this h"
       & "eading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper colwidths-auto docutils container"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table class=""docutils align-default"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><th class=""head""><p>Code</p></th>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<th class=""head""><p>Meaning</p></th>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-even""><td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span"
       & " class=""pre"">0</span></code></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Success (DAL achieved, all checks pass, <code class=""docutils literal"
       & " notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--version</span></code>, man page installed/"
       & "up-to-date)</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span "
       & "class=""pre"">1</span></code></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>Compliance failure (DAL unmet, tests failing, a <code class=""docutils"
       & " literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--require-*</span></code> CI gate un"
       & "met, differential regression, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><sp"
       & "an class=""pre"">man</span> <span class=""pre"">--check</span></code> finding a "
       & "newer version available or none installed, and more)</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""terminal-colour"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Terminal colour<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#terminal-colour"" title=""Link"
       & " to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex colours its terminal output (red for failures, green for passes,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "bold for headings) so the important lines stand out.  Colour is enabled by"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "default on a normal terminal.  It is suppressed automatically when the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "output would not take it:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">NO_COLOR"
       & "</span></code> is set (the cross-tool opt-out convention);</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p>a CI variable is set (GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, and more), so CI log"
       & "s"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "stay plain and machine-readable;</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">TERM</sp"
       & "an></code> is <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">d"
       & "umb</span></code> (or set to an empty value).</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""the-sbom-subcommand"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>The <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">sbom</s"
       & "pan></code> subcommand<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#the-sbom-subcommand"" titl"
       & "e=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">adacovex</sp"
       & "an> <span class=""pre"">sbom</span></code> resolves the target project"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s dependency graph from its Alire"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "manifest, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">alire"
       & "/alire.lock</span></code>, and the root <code class=""docutils literal notran"
       & "slate""><span class=""pre"">.gpr</span></code> <code class=""docutils literal no"
       & "translate""><span class=""pre"">with</span></code> clauses, then writes"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "a proof-aware software bill of materials in CycloneDX 1.5 JSON or SPDX 2.3"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "JSON. It is <strong>standard-aware</strong> (it defaults to all standards), "
       & "honours"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">SOURCE_DATE_EPO"
       & "CH</span></code> for byte-for-byte deterministic output, and is mutually"
