       & "he width allocated to the diagram (it takes up the same space the dependency"
       & " tree would, rather than shrinking to the graph"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s natural size) and is centred horizontally inside <code class=""docutils lit"
       & "eral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.nomnoml-wrap</span></code>; deep graphs"
       & " scroll inside the card.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Scope checkboxes filter the diagram too (re-render on change). Buttons <s"
       & "trong>Re-render</strong> and <strong>Download SVG</strong> are provided. The"
       & " view choice is persisted in <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><spa"
       & "n class=""pre"">localStorage</span></code> (<code class=""docutils literal notr"
       & "anslate""><span class=""pre"">adacovex-dep-view</span></code>).  <strong>Click "
       & "a box</strong> to open the same split-view detail panel as the Tree view.</p"
       & ">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>Two separate searches, similar styling</strong>:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Global search</strong> (header, <code class=""docutils literal"
       & " notranslate""><span class=""pre"">#global-search</span></code>) is a site-wide"
       & " <strong>section"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "index</strong>: at page load it walks the rendered DOM and indexes each sect"
       & "ion "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & ASCII.LF
       & "every metric card (labelled by its heading), every compliance-table row,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "every dependency node, and every HLR-tagged element "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " plus one catch-all"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "entry per tab.  Queries are tokenised and every token must appear in a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "section"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s lowercased text (AND semantics), so multi-word page text such as"
       & ASCII.LF
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "orphan tags"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " or a section heading like "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(156)
       & "Proof Check Types"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(157)
       & " resolves"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "regardless of case.  Selecting a hit switches to that tab and scrolls to"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(briefly flashing) the exact section, rather than only switching tabs."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Dependency names, versions, scopes, licences and PURLs are indexed too, so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the box still filters the dependency tree and seeds <code class=""docutils li"
       & "teral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">dep-filter</span></code>.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Tree filter</strong> (<code class=""docutils literal notransla"
       & "te""><span class=""pre"">#dep-filter</span></code>, inside the Dependencies tab"
       & ") is a plain"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "client-side name filter over the rendered tree only "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " it never touches the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "global index.  The two inputs share the same styling class so they look"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "consistent, but they are functionally independent (typing in one does not"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "affect the other until a global hit is clicked).</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The same data is available headlessly at <code class=""docutils literal no"
       & "translate""><span class=""pre"">/api/deps</span></code> and via"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--emit-metrics="
       & "PATH</span></code> (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class="""
       & "pre"">{&quot;metrics&quot;:...,</span> <span class=""pre"">&quot;dependencies&q"
       & "uot;:...}</span></code>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""metrics-charts"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h3>Metrics charts<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#metrics-charts"" title=""Link t"
       & "o this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h3>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <strong>Charts</strong> tab renders eight cards and is a <strong>stri"
       & "ct superset</strong> of the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Overview charts: every chart that appears on the Overview also appears"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "here. The charts are hand-rolled (no vendored chart library): donut rings"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "are a conic gradient with a CSS hole (the same pattern as the polar ring)"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "and bars are flex rows with a fixed label column, so labels never rotate"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "or overflow and the ring colour reflects the covered share (fully green at"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "100%):</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Robustness</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the five-axis health radar (Docs, Proof, Tests, Comp,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Deps) with the S/A/B/C/D tier rating, the same headline visual as the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Overview tab. It is shared with the Overview (one source of truth), so"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "the Charts tab is a superset and the two tabs cannot drift apart.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>SPARK Proof by Check Type</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the per-category proof radar (Flow,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Init, Runtime, Assert, Func) shown on the Overview, also shared.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>SPARK Proof</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <em>donut</em> of proved vs unproved VCs (<code class=""docutils literal not"
       & "ranslate""><span class=""pre"">720/720</span></code> shows a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "full green ring. <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"
       & """>680/720</span></code> shows <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><sp"
       & "an class=""pre"">94%</span></code> green + <code class=""docutils literal notra"
       & "nslate""><span class=""pre"">6%</span></code> red unproved).</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Proof Check Types</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
