       & ASCII.LF
       & "        <article role=""main"" id=""furo-main-content"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "          <section id=""compliance-standards-do-178c-iso-26262-iec-62304"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h1>Compliance Standards (DO-178C / ISO 26262 / IEC 62304)<a class=""headerli"
       & "nk"" href=""#compliance-standards-do-178c-iso-26262-iec-62304"" title=""Link to "
       & "this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""what-are-these-standards"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>What are these standards?<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#what-are-these-sta"
       & "ndards"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>DO-178C</strong> is the avionics software standard. It defines ho"
       & "w to design,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "implement, verify, and certify software that flies airplanes. Every line of"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "safety-critical flight software is assessed at one of five <strong>DAL</stro"
       & "ng> (Development"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "Assurance Level) tiers, from <strong>DAL-E</strong> (no safety effect) to <s"
       & "trong>DAL-A</strong>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(catastrophic failure can bring down the aircraft).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>ISO 26262</strong> is the automotive functional-safety standard. "
       & "It applies the same"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "rigor to road-vehicle software (braking, steering, powertrain). Its integrit"
       & "y"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "levels are called <strong>ASIL</strong> (Automotive Safety Integrity Level),"
       & " from <strong>QM</strong>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "(quality management, no hazard) to <strong>ASIL D</strong> (highest hazard)."
       & "</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>IEC 62304</strong> is the medical-device software lifecycle stand"
       & "ard. It classifies"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "software into <strong>safety classes</strong> A, B, and C based on the sever"
       & "ity of harm a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "failure can cause.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>All three demand the same underlying evidence:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol class=""arabic simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Requirement traceability</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " every high-level requirement (HLR) is traced"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "by a <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--</span> "
       & "<span class=""pre"">HLR-XXXX</span></code> tag in source.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>No orphan tags</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " every tag in source maps to a defined HLR.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Tests passing</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the test suite has zero failures (except at the lowest"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "tier).</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Minimum SPARK level</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the formal-proof bar for the selected rigor tier.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex computes all four checks once and re-labels the result per stand"
       & "ard."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "The same inputs feed the same outputs. Only the integrity-level label change"
       & "s.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""when-to-use-which-standard"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>When to use which standard<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#when-to-use-which"
       & "-standard"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper colwidths-auto docutils container"">"
       & ASCII.LF
