       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""assessment-criteria-shared"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Assessment criteria (shared)<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#assessment-crit"
       & "eria-shared"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The four checks stay identical across standards. Only the names change:</"
       & "p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ol class=""arabic simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Requirement traceability</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " every HLR defined in"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">docs/compliance"
       & "/HLR.md</span></code> is traced by a <code class=""docutils literal notransla"
       & "te""><span class=""pre"">--</span> <span class=""pre"">HLR-XXXX</span></code> tag"
       & " in source.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>No orphan tags</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " every in-source HLR maps to a defined HLR.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Tests passing</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " zero failures (not enforced at the lowest tier).</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Minimum SPARK level</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " the proof bar for the selected rigor tier.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ol>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Because the checks are shared, <strong>the compliance artifacts are ident"
       & "ical too</strong>:"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "ISO 26262 and IEC 62304 require no different evidence or documents than"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "DO-178C. The same inputs (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span c"
       & "lass=""pre"">HLR.md</span></code>, source traceability, proof summary, test"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "summary) feed the same outputs (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><"
       & "span class=""pre"">VERIFICATION.md</span></code>, <code class=""docutils litera"
       & "l notranslate""><span class=""pre"">TRACE.md</span></code>, the"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "proof-aware SBOM, and the compliance SVG badges) for every standard. Only th"
       & "e"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "integrity-level label printed inside them changes (<code class=""docutils lit"
       & "eral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">DAL-C</span></code>, <code class=""docuti"
       & "ls literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">ASIL</span> <span class=""pre"">B</s"
       & "pan></code>,"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">Class</span> <s"
       & "pan class=""pre"">A</span></code>).</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""selecting-a-standard-on-the-cli"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Selecting a standard on the CLI<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#selecting-a-"
       & "standard-on-the-cli"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Each standard has a dedicated level flag, so your intent is unambiguous o"
       & "n the"
       & ASCII.LF
