       & "          <section id=""vcs-support-and-differential-assessment"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h1>VCS support and differential assessment<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#vcs-"
       & "support-and-differential-assessment"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h1>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>A version control system is not required for base adacovex functi"
       & "onality.</strong></p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>This covers scanning, proof analysis, test parsing, compliance assessment"
       & ", SBOM generation, dashboards, and caching.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>A VCS is only needed for the differential modes below. They snapshot a ba"
       & "se revision to compare against the current tree.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>We assume that the audited project lives in a VCS. The base tool never re"
       & "quires one.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>adacovex works on <strong>Linux and WSL</strong>. The snapshot commands r"
       & "un through <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">sh</"
       & "span> <span class=""pre"">-c</span></code>, which WSL provides.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""when-to-use-differential-modes"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>When to use differential modes<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#when-to-use-d"
       & "ifferential-modes"" title=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Differential modes are useful when you want to enforce that changes do no"
       & "t regress quality gates:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>PR checks</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--coverage-del"
       & "ta</span></code> makes sure that docstring coverage does not drop between th"
       & "e base branch and the PR head. This is the lightest check. It works even whe"
       & "n the base does not commit proof or test artifacts.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Release gates</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">adacovex</span"
       & "> <span class=""pre"">--compare-base=v1.2.0</span></code> compares the current"
       & " tree against the last release tag. It fails if a metric regressed. These me"
       & "trics are packages, docstrings, HLR tags, SPARK level, tests, and DAL status"
       & ".</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Audit trails</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " a side-by-side report shows exactly what changed between two revisions. Thi"
       & "s is useful for compliance audits that need a narrative diff.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""supported-vcs"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2>Supported VCS<a class=""headerlink"" href=""#supported-vcs"" title=""Link to "
       & "this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The differential modes run against the VCS that manages the target. Detec"
       & "tion is marker-file based, with a command-probe fallback:</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<div class=""table-wrapper colwidths-auto docutils container"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<table class=""docutils align-default"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><th class=""head""><p>VCS</p></th>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<th class=""head""><p>Marker</p></th>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<th class=""head""><p>Base snapshot mechanism</p></th>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</thead>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-even""><td><p>git</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.git</sp"
       & "an></code></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">git</spa"
       & "n> <span class=""pre"">worktree</span> <span class=""pre"">add</span> <span clas"
       & "s=""pre"">--detach</span></code> (linked worktree)</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><td><p>jj</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.jj</spa"
       & "n></code></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">jj</span"
       & "> <span class=""pre"">git</span> <span class=""pre"">export</span></code> into t"
       & "he internal git store, then a git worktree against <code class=""docutils lit"
       & "eral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.jj/repo/store/git</span></code> (jj com"
       & "mits are git commits)</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-even""><td><p>Mercurial</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.hg</spa"
       & "n></code></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">hg</span"
       & "> <span class=""pre"">archive</span> <span class=""pre"">-r</span> <span class="""
       & "pre"">REF</span> <span class=""pre"">DIR</span></code> (pure export)</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-odd""><td><p>Subversion</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.svn</sp"
       & "an></code></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">svn</spa"
       & "n> <span class=""pre"">info</span> <span class=""pre"">--show-item</span> <span "
       & "class=""pre"">url</span></code> + <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><"
       & "span class=""pre"">svn</span> <span class=""pre"">export</span> <span class=""pre"
       & """>-r</span> <span class=""pre"">REF</span> <span class=""pre"">URL</span> <span "
       & "class=""pre"">DIR</span></code></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<tr class=""row-even""><td><p>Fossil</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">.fslckou"
       & "t</span></code> / <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pr"
       & "e"">_FOSSIL_</span></code></p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<td><p>copy the repo DB and <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span"
       & " class=""pre"">fossil</span> <span class=""pre"">open</span></code> it at REF in"
       & " a scratch dir</p></td>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tr>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</tbody>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</table>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</div>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>For colocated git+jj repos, git wins (exact interop). All snapshots land "
       & "in <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">/tmp/adacove"
       & "x-diff-&lt;pid&gt;</span></code> and are cleaned up afterwards. The working "
       & "tree is never touched.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><strong>UX recommendation</strong>: Git gives the best experience. Jj is "
       & "its git-compatible sibling. Mercurial is fully supported. For VCS whose snap"
       & "shot UX is poor, adacovex prints a note. The note recommends that developers"
       & " convert the repository to git (or a git-compatible VCS):</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<ul class=""simple"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Subversion</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " no local history, network-dependent checkouts, slow <code class=""docutils l"
       & "iteral notranslate""><span class=""pre"">svn</span> <span class=""pre"">export</s"
       & "pan></code> per snapshot. Converting gives local branches, offline history, "
       & "and faster diffs.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<li><p><strong>Fossil</strong> "
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(147)
       & " workable, but the tooling is niche and the single-file DB model complicates"
       & " CI integration.</p></li>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</ul>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>These notes are informational only. The assessment still runs and gates s"
       & "till apply on every supported VCS.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">adacovex</sp"
       & "an> <span class=""pre"">status</span></code> reports the VCS command-line tool"
       & "s on <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">$PATH</spa"
       & "n></code>. These tools are git, mercurial/<code class=""docutils literal notr"
       & "anslate""><span class=""pre"">hg</span></code>, subversion/<code class=""docutil"
       & "s literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">svn</span></code>, fossil, jj, and "
       & "<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">mandb</span></c"
       & "ode>. It reports the VCS detected for the target repository. It prints a not"
       & "e when the target"
       & Character'Val(226)
       & Character'Val(128)
       & Character'Val(153)
       & "s VCS tool is missing.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>See <a class=""reference internal"" href=""platforms.html#status-subcommand"""
       & "><span class=""std std-ref"">Platforms</span></a>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""compare-base-ref"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--compare-b"
       & "ase=REF</span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#compare-base-ref"" title=""L"
       & "ink to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Differential mode: adacovex snapshots a base revision in a temporary dire"
       & "ctory (<code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">/tmp/ada"
       & "covex-diff-&lt;pid&gt;</span></code>). It prints a side-by-side comparison a"
       & "gainst the current tree. The comparison shows packages, subprograms, docstri"
       & "ng percentage, traced HLR, orphan tags, SPARK level, proved VCs, tests, and "
       & "DAL status.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--target"
       & "</span></code> directory must be a supported VCS repository. The VCS command"
       & "-line tool must be on <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class"
       & "=""pre"">PATH</span></code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Exit <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">0</span"
       & "></code> only if there are no regressions and the current DAL is Achieved. O"
       & "therwise, exit <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">"
       & "1</span></code>. Artifacts that the base does not commit report <code class="
       & """docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">N/A</span></code> and are n"
       & "ot compared. These artifacts are <code class=""docutils literal notranslate"">"
       & "<span class=""pre"">gnatprove.out</span></code> and a test-result summary.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<section id=""coverage-delta-ref"">"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<h2><code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--coverage-"
       & "delta=REF</span></code><a class=""headerlink"" href=""#coverage-delta-ref"" titl"
       & "e=""Link to this heading"">"
       & Character'Val(194)
       & Character'Val(182)
       & "</a></h2>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Lightweight docstring-coverage gate for PR-style CI checks. It scans sour"
       & "ces, patches, and computes docstring metrics on a base revision and the curr"
       & "ent tree. It does not use GNATprove, tests, or DAL. Thus it works when the b"
       & "ase does not commit build artifacts.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>It prints a compact coverage table and a machine-parseable <code class=""d"
       & "ocutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">coverage_delta:</span></code>"
       & " line. Then it cleans up the snapshot.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>Exit <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">0</span"
       & "></code> if the current docstring coverage is <code class=""docutils literal "
       & "notranslate""><span class=""pre"">&gt;=</span></code> the base. Exit <code clas"
       & "s=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">0</span></code> also if t"
       & "he base has no sources. Exit <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><spa"
       & "n class=""pre"">1</span></code> if coverage regressed. This mode is mutually e"
       & "xclusive with <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">-"
       & "-compare-base</span></code>.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "<p>The release workflow runs the same gate against the last release tag (a"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "maintainer-only step; the <a class=""reference internal"" href=""../contributin"
       & "g/developer-guide.html""><span class=""std std-doc"">developer guide</span></a>"
       & " covers it)."
       & ASCII.LF
       & "For example, <code class=""docutils literal notranslate""><span class=""pre"">--"
       & "coverage-delta=v1.1.0</span></code> aborts if docstring coverage regressed"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "between two tags you compare at the command line.</p>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & "</section>"
       & ASCII.LF
       & ""
